h means he's not going to win the state. But he's running significantly better than he did the other times that he ran. And that to me is just - that is almost an across-the-board story line tonight, that places where, whether it's blue or red, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has beaten his number by a little bit.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Not only beaten his number from last time, but beat his number when he ran against \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2  in 2016. He's outperforming in some of these counties. Let's head up to Rhode Island, New Hampshire, some of these other states that typically we would call earlier in the night.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RHODE ISLAND\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Rhode Island is projected now, but it was closer than it should have been by all rights, and you see some more working class parts of the state tending to do a little bit redder. Even in the capital of Providence, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  not quite, not quite \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's numbers. You start to see that kind of erosion, that slippage. It doesn't really matter where it is. Yeah, New Hampshire, we haven't had a projection yet. We're - talking about a 20,000 vote margin in a state that gets a lot of political attention. A lot of the Democratic votes are here in the southern part. We have to wait to see if we get more, about half of it in so far. But the earlier point still holds, that places where Democrats should - get a projection pretty early, Connecticut and New Jersey, - she's win New Jersey, but the fact that we'd even mention it on air on an election night, a Connecticut on air, a 24,000 vote margin, tells you that there's something that she hasn't really been able to bring out her base in places that don't get a lot of attention in a presidential (inaudible)...\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, the Democratic base. And it's a question of what kind of coalition, if she's able to pull this off, did she put together in order to pull it off. And if not, the questions will be, why wasn't she able to pull it off. Show us in each one of these three blue wall states, the map that shows us the outstanding vote, the percentage of the vote.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PENNSYLVANIA\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sure, - start here in Pennsylvania again, down 120,000 votes. That's Philadelphia and the eastern suburbs. A little bit in Pittsburgh. Places like Harrisburg, State College, Erie, they're 50/50 splits or close to it. So you're not going to net as much either way. That's the path that's still there and very much an existent path. I think Pennsylvania very realistic. Michigan, I mentioned how little vote is in Detroit right now. I think you'll see it come up in a very dramatic way there. Some of these bubbles overlap, because the counties are so close. And there's just a lot of vote that's left there. Harris right now, we see some new numbers, it's 100,000 votes or so, and Wisconsin, again, Milwaukee is just going to be huge here. Madison, most of the vote is already in, in a heavily Democratic place. Right now it's only about 3,000 votes as the numbers continue to roll in.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I know, Rachel, you've been diving into some of these college towns, this is gonna be something we look at later, how young voters split if the gender gap was what we think it could be potentially going into election night. What are you seeing?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, we know Vice President Kamala Harris and former president Donald Trump, quite frankly, trying to get young male voters to turn out. Vice President Kamala Harris trying to get younger voters to turn out in general. La Crosse, home to three different colleges, thousands of students. Let's take a look at how she's doing here. 52% of the vote. She's ahead by 3,000, 3,500 votes so far. She's pretty much almost where President Biden was, with 71% of the vote in. Eau Claire, another one, take a look here, she's still leading in this county as well, ahead by 4,000.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm just checking the benchmark. I'm just so curious of where, where, she's just slightly under where FiveThirtyEight thought she should be. Can you show us, let's go back to La Crosse just for a second. She's just under where she needs to be in these college towns. Where else were you looking?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also in Madison. Dane County, this has high voter turnout here. You still have 89% of the vote in. 90% of this county turns out to vote. I don't know where that happens anywhere else in America. But she's going to need to do well here. And then of course, Waukesha, for former president Donald Trump, going to be absolutely critical. This just (inaudible) a Republican has to go super Republican. This is really where he has to super energize his base, and then also, you know, Rick was talking about Milwaukee. Former president Donald Trump campaigning here also multiple times. Look, traditionally, yes, this does go towards Democrats, of course. Vice President Kamala Harris right now, 66%. Let's see where she is with the FiveThirtyEight benchmark.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just under, yeah.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Just under that, right now. But former president Donald Trump, Waukesha is where he earns the most votes. 2016, 2020, the second highest for him is Milwaukee. So he still has to run up the score in Milwaukee in order to do well.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Al right, this is the key number at this hour, 6,500 votes between them. Donald Trump leading in Wisconsin tonight. We're going to keep our eye on all three of these states. Wisconsin, Michigan, Pennsylvania. Don't go away. We'll dive into these numbers even more right after the break.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KANSAS PROJECTED WINNER, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEBRASKA PROJECTED WINNER, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 This is ABC News coverage of election night 2024. Here again, David Muir.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back to ABC News live coverage of election night here. We do want to call another state. Kansas, the six electoral votes of Kansas will go to former president Trump. In Nebraska tonight, Donald Trump picks up three electoral votes, and John Karl, explain to the audience how that works in Nebraska, they split these up.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They split them up by congressional district and then overall winner. So there is a single electoral vote coming out of Nebraska, it's in Omaha. Sometimes they call it Obamaha, because Obama won it, helped him win the presidency in 2008. So look, if we're looking at a scenario where Kamala Harris's path to winning the presidency is to win the blue wall and not to win any of the other battleground states in the Sun Belt, it would be 270 votes to 268 votes, the single vote that would put her over the top would be in Omaha. It would be that split electoral vote in the state of Nebraska. Of course we've got a long way to go tonight before we get to that point.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do, we do.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But that's why Republicans tried to change the rules in Nebraska. Lindsey Graham made a trip all the way out to Nebraska to try to convince...\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This election cycle.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...yes, this election cycle. Donald Trump got involved. He called some of the state - legislators to try to get them to change the rules there. They didn't change the rules, and that could be a very pivotal, single electoral vote.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Could be, could be, but it's early.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's early, we've got a long way to go.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So let's go back to some of these Senate races. We want to call a few more races here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE NEW JERSEY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE VIRGINIA\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In New Jersey, we can call the Senate race now for the Democrat, Congressman Andy Kim. Three term congressman running for Senate. He wins. He's going to now take over the seat that was once held by Robert Menendez, until he was convicted. So Congressman Andy Kim wins in New Jersey. In Virginia, seeking a third term, Senator Tim Kaine has been reelected in Virginia, though the race has not been called in Virginia on the presidential level, which is quite extraordinary for this time of the night.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE TEXAS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In Texas at this hour, we can say Republican Senator Ted Cruz, who was seeking a third term, has been reelected to the Senate. He'd been challenged by Congressman Colin Allred, of course, from Baylor University, Tennessee Titans football player, three term congressman himself. He had campaigned on so many issues, reproductive rights one of them. Linsey, you interviewed him in just the last week or two. And Democrats really thought he had some prospects there. They were putting some late money into the campaign.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As you know, David, football is a little bit more of a popular pastime in Texas than politics is. And Colin Allred really staked a lot on that. Even his campaign ads really started on the football field, ended on the football field. He talked about how he'd taken down a lot tougher opponents than Ted Cruz before. But look, this really was an uphill battle for him. It's been 30 years, to election day, when a Democrat was able to win a statewide position in the state of Texas. And so really, this was a fierce, it shouldn't have been, really, when you think about it, but Ted Cruz has a pretty high unpopularity rate in the state of Texas. But for Colin Allred, this was really a disappointment, he actually thought that he was going to be able to do it. And do want to give a shout out to Andy Kim, the first Korean American to ever be a US Senator.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now he's represent New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No question. Let's get right to John Quinones, on the ground in Texas. John, what do you make of the news?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS\par \par \uc2 JOHN QUINONES (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, this is one of the most closely watched races in the country, David, the incumbent Republican, Ted Cruz, once a presidential candidate himself, challenged by three term Democratic Congressman and former, like Linsey said, former NFL linebacker, Colin Allred. They campaigned bitterly in the state over women's reproductive rights, the border, transgender rights. Cruz calling Allred too liberal for Texas. In the end, amidst a changing political landscape here in Texas, Ted Cruz survived the challenge just a few minutes ago. In his victory speech, Cruz specifically thanked Latino voters in the state, which he says have proven all the political prognosticators wrong.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) John Quinones on the ground there in Texas, John, thank you. Look at the margin there. That's a much bigger margin than even Beto O'Rourke when he took on Ted Cruz, came almost within two points of defeating Ted Cruz, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, within two points, much bigger margin this time, and that is because Colin Allred really underperformed in some of the big cities. So let's take Harris County, this is home to Houston. You can see the FiveThirtyEight benchmark that we have, has him at 58. He got 53. Let's go over to Austin. This is Travis County. 74% is what he needed to meet. 71 is where he was. David, I will tell you, Linsey already said it. But you know, Ted Cruz, deeply unpopular, even in his own state. He's tried to rebrand his image to be more approachable and be more bipartisan. I don't think there's anywhere else in this country where Cancun was talked about more than in this state. You remember those images of Ted Cruz at the airport after that deadly winter storm. Colin Allred ran ad after ad on that. But ultimately, Ted Cruz remained victorious in this state.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rick Klein, you've over at the big board as well. What are you seeing in some of these key battlegrounds. How's Pennsylvania looking at this hour?\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Pennsylvania right now is still a problem for Kamala Harris. And advantage Donald Trump, 100,000 vote margin. A lot left of the vote, and - some of these bubbles will tell you the story about what's left. 175,000 votes left in Philadelphia is our estimate. Another 193,000 in Delaware County, Delco, a place where Harris is winning very big. Bucks County, still a lot of votes to be counted there, 240,000. So that's what's keeping this as a competitive state right now. But we've seen the numbers shift as more of the Republican parts of the state have fallen in line for Donald Trump. It's been almost, almost consistent across the board. Again, not the biggest counties, but places where he's been able to build on his lead consistently.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I think that's a good example when you pulled up Perry County. Just look at the threshold, the FiveThirtyEight threshold of where he needs to be. And this is the story of the night, he's outperforming slightly in all these rural counties. I think we're seeing this in a number of the swing states, which is helping him to build these margins against Kamala Harris.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's exactly right. And it adds up over time. And I think that's - similar to what we've seen in Michigan, - Wisconsin. Michigan doesn't have a lot of vote in right now. But you're seeing some areas where Donald Trump in the past has not particularly, not been that strong. This is more of a swingy type county. You can see where Joe Biden was. You can see where Kamala Harris is. You see where Donald Trump was, you see where he is right now. And in many cases, it's that he's beating himself twice over. This guy's been on the ballot a lot.\par \par \uc2 RICK KLEIN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Voters have had the opportunity to vote for him or vote against him several times now. So, again, it's not the big urban areas. That's going to go pretty Democratic, and it's still possible that Harris pulls out enough of the vote in Madison and Milwaukee, where we're still waiting on vote. But it becomes difficult as time goes by, and that really is the story that's developing now in North Carolina. When we look at our remaining votes, these blue dots have been getting smaller throughout the night. When you really get into it, you're talking about 115,000 votes, okay, - if you win that 2 to 1, you start to chip away at that 145,000 vote lead, but there may not be enough of those blue dots left in a Georgia or a North Carolina, based on what we're seeing tonight.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, we're gonna continue to drill down on these, on these blue wall states with Rick Klein and Rachel Scott over at the board. We're closing in on 11:00 here in the east, 8:00 in the west. Four more states set to close, including California, with its 54 electoral votes. Your local news is next. And we'll see you just minutes from now with more numbers coming in, including the Sun Belt states. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 Document ABSR000020241122ekb500002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAKING DOWN THE CRITICAL ISSUES ABORTION ON THE BALLOT & THE GENDER GAP\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, ELECTION, POLLS, EARLY VOTES\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, EXPLOSIVE DEVICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, SECURITY, YATES, RAFFENSPERGER, SKINNER, KRASNER\par \par \uc2 ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DECISION DAY IN THE RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS & TRUMP FIGHT TO THE FINISH AS POLLS OPEN\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLEGROUND NORTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE HELENE'S AFTERMATH NOT STOPPING VOTERS IN KEY STATE\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLEGROUND ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF THE TEN STATES WHERE ABORTION IS ON THE BALLOT\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOTING RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO KNOW BEFORE HEADING TO THE POLLS\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, ELECTION, PENNSYLVANIA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS SPRINTS TO THE FINISH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VICE PRESIDENT MAKES FINAL PITCH TO VOTERS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ELECTION, PALM BEACH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP'S FINAL PUSH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT HITS THREE BATTLEGROUNDS\par \par \uc2 BOEING, STRIKE, NEGOTIATION, OFFER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BOEING STRIKE ENDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: UNION ACCEPTS NEW CONTRACT OFFER\par \par \uc2 CHIEFS, BUCCANEERS, FOOTBALL, UNDEFEATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHIEFS STAY UNDEFEATED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KANSAS CITY BEATS BUCCANEERS IN OVERTIME THRILLER\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY, ELECTION, TRUMP, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN THE CRITICAL ISSUES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE ECONOMY & THE CANDIDATES' PLANS\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, BALLOT, ARIZONA, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN THE CRITICAL ISSUES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ON THE BALLOT & THE GENDER GAP\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we go to Elizabeth Schulze, who has more on the issue abortion and what both Trump and Harris have said about that. Good morning to you again, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning again, Robin. Polls are now open here in Arizona, where voters will decide if the right to an abortion should be enshrined in the state's constitution. This is one of 10 states with a ballot initiative to expand ballot initiative to expand abortion access. In every state where abortion has been on the ballot since the end of Roe v Wade, including in red states, the abortion rights position has won. And that helps explain why we've seen former President Trump change his position on this. He had supported a national abortion ban, now says it is up to the states.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Vice President Harris is hammering Trump for appointing three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe, and we know it's mobilizing women voters. Our latest ABC News/Ipsos poll shows that Harris has an 11-point advantage over Trump among women. Harris hopes that by putting reproductive rights at the center of her campaign, she can edge out Trump\u160\'00\'A0in critical battlegrounds, like here in Arizona, Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Definitely a big issue there. Elizabeth, thank you so much for that.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241122ekb50003d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BATTLEGROUND ARIZONA ONE OF THE TEN STATES WHERE ABORTION IS ON THE BALLOT\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, ELECTION, POLLS, EARLY VOTES\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, EXPLOSIVE DEVICES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, SECURITY, YATES, RAFFENSPERGER, SKINNER, KRASNER\par \par \uc2 ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DECISION DAY IN THE RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS & TRUMP FIGHT TO THE FINISH AS POLLS OPEN\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLEGROUND NORTH CAROLINA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE HELENE'S AFTERMATH NOT STOPPING VOTERS IN KEY STATE\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLEGROUND ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE OF THE TEN STATES WHERE ABORTION IS ON THE BALLOT\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And now to Arizona where abortion is on the ballot. Elizabeth Schulze is in Phoenix for us. Good morning to you, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Robin. Voters here in Maricopa County know that their ballots will likely decide who wins Arizona's 11 electoral votes and will also decide if the right to an abortion should be enshrined in Arizona's Constitution.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ON THE BALLOT\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is one of ten states with a ballot initiative to expand abortion access. Organizers behind the Arizona's measure tell us they are confident that it will pass, but that doesn't guarantee a win here for Vice President Harris. They do expect that many voters will split the ticket and still vote for former President Trump. Election officials in Maricopa County are bracing for a tight race. We've got a look inside the center where 60% of Arizona's ballots will be counted. It is a meticulous process in every step, from unsealing the ballots to verifying signatures, to tabulating votes. Republicans and Democrats team up to supervise.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It took them ten days to count the votes in 2020. And this year, election officials say it could take even longer. George?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Elizabeth, thanks very much. Coming up next, what you need to know before you head out to the polls.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Dan Abrams\uc2  is here breaking down your rights as a voter.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241122ekb500034\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ABORTION ON THE BALLOT RESIDENTS IN TEN STATES TO VOTE ON INITIATIVES EXPANDING ABORTION RIGHTS\b0\par\par\uc2 415 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP BARNSTORMS THE BATTLEGROUNDS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CAMPAIGN, RALLIES, RHETORIC, 2020, RFK\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, CAMPAIGN, BATTLEGROUNDS, VOTERS, "SNL"\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, POLLS, HARRIS, TRUMP, GENDER, DIVISION\par \par \uc2 CAMPAIGNS, TRUMP, RHETORIC, BATTLEGROUNDS, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, SECURITY, POLL WORKERS, DISINFORMATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOOD THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, VOTING, GEORGIA, POLLS\par \par \uc2 CAMPAIGN, HARRIS, BATTLEGROUND, BLUE WALL, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, ARIZONA, ABORTION, POLLS, WORKER, SECURITY\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, Robin. Abortion is also on the ballot in 10 states, including the battleground state of Arizona. And Elizabeth Schulze is in Phoenix with more. Good morning, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION ON THE BALLOT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RESIDENT IN TEN STATES TO VOTE ON INITIATIVES EXPANDING ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning, Rebecca. We are right outside of the Maricopa County Election Center where 60% of all of Arizona's ballots will be counted, and directly on those ballots is abortion. Arizona is one of 10 states with an ballot initiative to expand abortion rights. The proposition here would enshrine the right to an abortion in Arizona's constitution.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And organizers tell us they are optimistic that it will pass with bipartisan support. At the top of the ticket, this is a tight race with former President Trump slightly ahead. He narrowly lost to President Biden here by just 10,000 votes in 2020. And, Rebecca, that was the first win for a Democrat since 1996.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLEGROUND ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SECURITY MEASURES AFTER CLOSE FINISH IN 2020 THREATS TO ELECTION WORKERS\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, Elizabeth, we saw the tight race in 2020 play out with protests and conspiracy theories there. What does security look like this time around?\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And this center really was the target of some of these protest from Trump supporters and election deniers. Some workers here tell us they're actually still facing violent threats on their lives. So you can see entire this iron fence, that was put up after the 2020 election.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's another fence outside of the perimeter of the building. And the sheriff's office tells us they've all put in place snipers, patrols on horseback, drones, just for extra surveillance too, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Deep appreciation for all the people doing that work there. Okay, Elizabeth, thank you. Robin.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241122ekb40000b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BATTLE FOR ARIZONA IMMIGRATION AND ABORTION RIGHTS DRIVING VOTER TURNOUT\b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Sunday\par \uc2 WNSU\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , RALLIES, RHETORIC, POLLS, RFK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP: SHOULDN'T HAVE LEFT WHITE HOUSE IN 2020\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, HARRIS, VOTERS, "SNL", CAMPAIGN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINAL PUSH FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, NY USA/PHILADELPHIA, PA USA\par \par \uc2 PENNSYLVANIA, CAMPAIGN, CANDIDATES, BALLOTS, SHAPIRO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE FOR PENNSYLVANIA\par \par \uc2 CAMPAIGN, GEORGIA, VOTING, SAFEGUARDS, FRAUD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE FOR GEORGIA\par \par \uc2 CAMPAIGN, ARIZONA, IMMIGRATION, ABORTION, TURNOUT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE FOR ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Georgia on our mind once again. Faith, thank you. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze is in Phoenix, Arizona, which is a state President Biden won in 2020, but is now up for grabs. Elizabeth, what are you seeing there on the ground?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLE FOR ARIZONA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IMMIGRATION AND ABORTION RIGHTS DROVING VOTER TURNOUT\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Linsey, election officials here tell me they are bracing for a very tight race between former President Trump and Vice President Harris. Both of their running mates campaigning here this weekend. Senator Vance making his pitch in the pivotal Phoenix suburbs. And Governor Walz courting young voters and women.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Arizona is one of 10 states where abortion will be on the ballot. Voters here will decide if the right to an abortion should be enshrined in the state's constitution. The Harris campaign is banking on that driving voter turnout. President Biden won this state by only 10,000 votes in 2020. Linsey.\par \par \uc2 Document WNSU000020241105ekb300006\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INVESTIGATION INTO PREGNANT TEXAS TEEN'S DEATH FAMILY SAYS 18-YEAR-OLD WAS DENIED MEDICAL CARE UNTIL IT WAS TOO LATE\b0\par\par\uc2 1,004 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 November 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEST COAST BLITZ\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, CAMPAIGN, RALLY, KENNEDY, PUERTO RICO, CHENEY\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, BATTLEGROUNDS, LOPEZ, LATINOS, WOMEN\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, POLLS, HARRIS, TRUMP, VOTING\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, INTERFERENCE, FOREIGN, EASTERLY, VIDEOS\par \par \uc2 JOBS, ECONOMY, ELECTION, FED, UNEMPLOYMENT\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, HALLOWEEN, DEAD, INJURED, SUSPECT\par \par \uc2 JETS, TEXANS, CATCH, ONE-HANDED, WILSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 PAYNE, DEATH, DRUGS, IMAGES, BALCONY, FALL\par \par \uc2 TRIAL, PENNY, NEELY, SUBWAY, CHOKEHOLD, COMINSKY, MAHAZU\par \par \uc2 STUDY, SUGAR, BABIES, PREGNANCY, DIABETES, BLOOD PRESSURE\par \par \uc2 THANKSGIVING, TURKEYS, MEAL, PRICES, DEMER\par \par \uc2 BILTMORE, HELENE, CHRISTMAS, REOPENS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRE DANGER\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, HARRIS, TRUMP\par \par \uc2 TEXAS, TEEN, PREGNANCY, DEATH\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now a new investigation from ProPublica into the case of a Texas teen who died of complications from her pregnancy after her family said the care she needed was denied until it was too late. Rachel Scott is back with the story. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael, good morning to you again. Yeah, Candice Bail said that she lost her 18-year-old daughter a year ago. She was six months pregnant when she started experiencing severe pregnancy complication. She went to the emergency room three separate times, but this morning her mother tells me she ultimately died because she could not get the care she desperately needed in a state with one of the strictest abortion bans.\par \par \uc2 CANDICE FAILS (MOTHER OF NEVAEH CRAIN)\par \par \uc2 She loved to sing. She loved to dance. She was a wonderful soul.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Candice Fails says her daughter, Navaeh, at six months pregnant, first started complaining of stomach pain and nausea. She went to the emergency room at Baptist Hospitals of Southeast Texas.\par \par \uc2 CANDICE FAILS (MOTHER OF NEVAEH CRAIN)\par \par \uc2 She's in a lot of pain. Her stomach is hurting her.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Candice says Nevaeh was diagnosed with strep throat and didn't even receive an ultrasound. She was sent back home. When the pain didn't go away, she went to the emergency room at Christus St. Elizabeth, but was told her fetus still had a heartbeat and that she was fine to leave. It wasn't until her third visit to the ER that she says doctors realizing something was terribly wrong, saying the fetus no longer had a heartbeat.\par \par \uc2 CANDICE FAILS (MOTHER OF NEVAEH CRAIN)\par \par \uc2 They were saying her blood pressure keeps dropping. She was losing blood. She was like, mom, I don't think I can do this. I was like, Nevaeh, I told her, I said, I love you. I said, you can do this. I said, god made us strong, you can do this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROPUBLICA REPORT\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) ProPublica releasing an article this morning after an investigation into her death, finding that it took 20 hours and three emergency room visits to be admitted to a hospital even though her condition was worsening. They say the doctors did two ultrasounds to confirm fetal demise.\par \par \uc2 CANDICE FAILS (MOTHER OF NEVAEH CRAIN)\par \par \uc2 And I'm hollering at them, I'm telling them to save my daughter. To save my daughter. Do something.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Candice says she believes her daughter didn't get the care she deserved to save her life because of the state's strict abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 CANDICE FAILS (MOTHER OF NEVAEH CRAIN)\par \par \uc2 I felt like the doctors were more concerned about the baby than her life. I'm frustrated how these laws are affecting my daughter from getting justice that she deserves.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOTHER BELIEVES STATE'S STRICT ABORTION BAN IS TO BLAME FOR DELAYED MEDICAL CARE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Christus St. Elizabeth told us it, quote, believes the care provided to this patient was at all times appropriate and compassionate. However, due to HIPAA and privacy, we cannot comment further. Baptist Hospitals of Southeast Texas did not respond.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, well ProPublica says that they reached out to the doctors involved and they did not respond to their requests for comment. Texas, of course, has one of the strictest abortion bans in the country. Does include a narrow exception to save the life of the mother, but we've talked to a lot of doctors in that state who say there's so much confusion around these laws that it has changed how and when they intervene. Of course, any doctor who performs an unlawful abortion in the state of Texas could face prison time, loss of license, and also some fines. This is just another ripple effect after Roe versus Wade was overturned, guys, but this mother, she is pleading for change this morning.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Rachel, thanks very much. Coming up in our "GMA" morning menu, Shawn Mendes on his decision to step away from the spotlight at the peak of his fame.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHAWN MENDES OPENS UP\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also ahead, these soon to be marathoners are ready to hit the ground running for the New York City Marathon.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: READY TO RUN!\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Plus Deals & Steals are all Oprah's favorite things. Tory Johnson is here with "Oprah Daily" creative director Adam Glassman with a dozen great products, and Sam has two special guests. Hey, Sam.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS: OPRAH'S FAVORITE THINGS\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well I haven't stopped talking to them, so I don't know if I'm really ready to introduce them. But we're here with Jennifer Grey and Jesse Eisenberg to talk all about what looks like a really great movie. Jesse, how are you feeling this hour?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JENNIFER GREY & JESSE EISENBERG LIVE!\par \par \uc2 JESSE EISENBERG ("A REAL PAIN")\par \par \uc2 I'm feeling exhausted watching these people run.\par \par \uc2 SAM CHAMPION (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. We'll sit down and have a chat when we come back right here on "GMA." Stay with us.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241119ekb10000j\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MOMBIE APOCALYPSE BREAST CANCER RESEARCH\b0\par\par\uc2 170 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 PRESLEY, LISA MARIE, GRACELAND, KEOUGH, PHILBRICK, RUSSELL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 STEWART, "MARTHA", CUTLER, CARTER, SELF-MADE, LIFESTYLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 MOMBIES, BREAST CANCER, FUNDRAISING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally, on this Halloween night, it's the mombie apocalypse.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A group of Connecticut moms dressing up and dancing for a good cause to Michael Jackson's "Thriller," raising money for breast cancer research.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They appeared on "World News Tonight" last year and raised $80,000. This year in new York City, performing "Stayin' Alive" by the Bee Gees, setting their fundraising sights even higher.\par \par \uc2 MOMBIE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 The ghouls on this mombie's express have raised over $500,000 for breast cancer research.\par \par \uc2 MOMBIES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 And we're just getting started.\par \par \uc2 PHIL LIPOF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Well done. Maybe next year even more. That's "Nightline." See you right back here tomorrow at the same time. Thanks for staying up with us. Good night, America.\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020241105ekav00004\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 POWER IN PINK SHANICE ON HER BREAST CANCER JOURNEY\b0\par\par\uc2 1,233 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS:: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KAMALA HARRIS' CLOSING ARGUMENT\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, SPEECH, ELLIPSE, CAMPAIGN, APPEAL\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , RALLY, MSG, BACKLASH, RACIST, RFK\par \par \uc2 ELECTION, BALLOT BOXES, FIRES, SECURITY, GATES, LOGAN\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, AIRSTRIKE, GAZA, DEAD, PALESTINIANS, \uc2 UN\par \par \uc2 WORLD SERIES, \uc2 YANKEES\uc2 , DODGERS, GAME 5\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, CLEMENCY, GOVERNOR, DA, CONVICTION\par \par \uc2 MURDER, ROSAS, HAMPTONS, RESORT, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 ROBINSON, MURDER, LAWSUIT, DOJ, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , COMPANIONS, MEXICO\par \par \uc2 GARR, CAREER, LEGACY, MOVIES, TV, MS\par \par \uc2 WORLD SERIES, \uc2 YANKEES\uc2 , FIREFIGHTER, DAUGHTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRE DANGER\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, WALZ\par \par \uc2 MENDES, SEXUALITY\par \par \uc2 KIDS, SCREEN TIME\par \par \uc2 "DANCING WITH THE STARS", "WICKED", GAYNOR, "I WILL SURVIVE \u8211\'20\'13 THE GLORIA GAYNOR STORY"\par \par \uc2 RUSSELL, "THE DIPLOMAT"\par \par \uc2 SHANICE, CANCER\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back, everybody. We were all singing along to that song back in the '90s. "I Love Your Smile" by our next guest, Grammy nominated singer actress Shanice. And she is, is on stage right now, appearing in "44" the musical about \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 . But she's here this morning for a very different reason. She was diagnosed with breast cancer in June. And now she's here to share her story. Shanice, thank you for being here.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHANICE ON HER BREAST CANCER JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much for having me.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's great to have you. So, so we're going to start back in March.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back in, back in March you, you felt a lump in your breast.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you went in for a mammogram, which is something you've been putting off for quite a while.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yeah, so eight years ago they thought they saw something because I have dense breasts. And so every time I get, you know, go for my test, they have to test me several times because my breasts, you know, was so dense. But, and they, and I had, I had a lot of cysts in my breast, like, prior. So eight years ago they thought they saw something. They wanted to do a biopsy. But then they said, no, it's fine, it's nothing, it's just a cyst. So because of the fear that I had when they thought they saw something, I didn't go for eight years. So, then I felt a lump in my breast and I'm like, this cyst isn't going away. I need to have this looked at. And I did the mammogram and the ultrasound and unfortunately they saw something. It was, it was cancer.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. So they, the doctors, they, they found cancer. But what did they tell you?\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Well, they first told me they saw that I had DCIS, which is stage zero, and it's in the milk ducts. So they say, it's great, it's just in the milk ducts. We'll just take your breasts out and you'll be fine. So then after I, I said well, I want both, if I have to have one breast removed, I'd rather do both. So they, we did both. After my surgery, they said, well, unfortunately you had a stage I, one centimeter tumor in your breast. So I found that out, actually, the end of May is when I had my surgery. And...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So you had the double mastectomy. When, and in the course of that, they found something else.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you say when that happened, you, you kind of, you know, your, your song, "I Love Your Smile" but this, at that point you say you lost your smile a little bit.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 I did. So in, in the, when I had my surgery and they told me I had cancer, I literally lost my smile. And, but I, I wanted to come on the show to encourage women that you have to keep smiling, you know? Like, I got my smile back.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good. Thank goodness.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 And I just want to tell women how important it is to get your mammograms and get your ultrasounds, like, yearly. If I would have gone, you know, sooner, I could have caught it when it was just at stage zero. So, you know, I just want to encourage women to do that. And I want to give a shout out to \uc2 City of Hope\uc2 . They did my surgery. Veronica Jones, Dr. Lee at \uc2 City of Hope\uc2  in Doherty. The, the great thing is that they removed my breasts but they were able to put in implants at the same time, so that was great.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and I love to hear, you're here to share your story because disproportionately this affects black women, and so I think for you being here and having them see you go through this hopefully will encourage more of them to go get checked.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Instead of, you know, you said you, the fear kept you away.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 The fear did. Yeah. And I just want to tell women out there that, you know, put that fear aside. If you, you know, get checked early, you can beat this thing. It's not a death sentence. You know? If you can just get there early, you'll, you'll live, so, and I, and I got to give a shout out to my husband because...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, the family...\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Support system from the family is the biggest thing. And I know your husband really well, and he, he loves you.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 I love him too.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He loves you, and your family supports you, and that's another message.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yes. Yes. I had the support of my family. So Flex, you know, after my surgery, he helped me, you know, clear out my drains and he gave me, he took, helped me take my showers. He made my meals. My, my kids were very supportive. My mom was, was there. You know, I had all my prayer warriors praying for me. So, yeah.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and I love what Robin said earlier when she said you were coming on the show. She goes, she's thriving.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yes, yes.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and, but we're happy that you're here sharing this story. I think you're gonna help a lot of women out there who may be hesitant about going to see their doctors.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yes. And I want to say that, I want everybody to keep their smile. I have a lipstick line called Smile by Shanice and, and I want, I want women to support it because I just, like, you know, I want to keep a smile on everyone's faces.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're smiling because you're here and sharing this with us.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Shanice, thank you.\par \par \uc2 SHANICE ("44")\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We really appreciate you being here.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241114ekau0000p\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG THE MOMBIES ARE BACK\b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP RIPS BIDEN'S "GARBAGE" COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TORNADO THREAT & RECORD HEAT\par \par \uc2 SPAIN, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLOODS KILL AT LEAST 95, TRAP THOUSANDS\par \par \uc2 MIDAIR ASSAULT, ARREST, MURDER, SPA, MENENDEZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRUTAL MID-FLIGHT ATTACK\par \par \uc2 WORLD SERIES, GRAMMY AWARDS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 MOMBIES, CANCER RESEARCH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: #AMERICASTRONG\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally tonight here, "America Strong." The MOMbies are back.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, with Halloween just about here, the moms are back. They're not zombies, they call themselves the MOMbies. Moms dressing up together, dancing on the Main Street in Fairfield, Connecticut, all for a good cause. Michael Jackson's "Thriller," raising money for breast cancer research.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And we learned today that after you met them right here last Halloween, they tell us "World News" viewers donated $80,000. And tonight, those MOMbies have a new message for you.\par \par \uc2 MOMBIES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Thank you, ABC.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And one year later, they're back, performing "Staying Alive" by the Bee Gees. Among them, Karen Sullivan (PH), battling stage four breast cancer, practicing during her chemotherapy treatments. And right here tonight.\par \par \uc2 PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Karen, that fighter, proud to call herself a mombie.\par \par \uc2 PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 The treatment I'm on did not exist in totality five years ago. That is the power of research. And that is why we dance.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Last year, you met Joy Martini (PH), this was her message then.\par \par \uc2 PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I'm a MOMbie and I'm also a breast cancer patient. And I couldn't be more grateful and more proud than dancing with these women.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This is joy now.\par \par \uc2 PATIENT (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey, David. This year, I'm a mombie with no evidence of disease.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We're so happy to hear it. And tonight, joining us, too\par \par \uc2 MOMBIE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Hey, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The mombies on their way to their next performance tonight. And just listen to how much money they've raised already.\par \par \uc2 MOMBIE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Over $500,000 for breast cancer research.\par \par \uc2 MOMBIES (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 And we're just getting started.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And they're just getting started. They're an inspiration. We love them. Thank you for watching here. I'm David Muir. I'll see you right back here tomorrow. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241101ekau00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE: NINE DAYS TO CLOSE THE DEAL \uc2 MICHELLE OBAMA\uc2  JOINS VP HARRIS, SPEAKS ON WOMEN'S HEALTH & TAKES AIM AT TRUMP\b0\par\par\uc2 840 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUCK SLAMS INTO ISRAELI CROWD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, BUS, CRASH, IRAN\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, OBAMA, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE: NINE DAYS TO CLOSE THE DEAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 MICHELLE OBAMA\uc2  JOINS VP HARRIS, SPEAKS ON WOMEN'S HEALTH & TAKES AIM AT \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Turning now to the presidential race, just nine days to go now. The candidates planning major events this week to deliver their closing message to voters.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Former President Trump holding a big rally inside New York's Madison Square Garden today. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on Tuesday takes to the National Mall in Washington. ABC's White House correspondent Maryalice Parks joins us with the latest. And, Maryalice, a familiar face hitting the trail as well for Vice President Harris. Good morning.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. That's right. Good morning, Whit. \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  said that she hates politics, but she felt the stakes were too high. She gave one of the most powerful speeches of the campaign cycle, describing in intimate detail the effects of new restrictions on reproductive health and asking men, in her words, to take women's lives seriously.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, \uc2 Michelle Obama\uc2  on the campaign trail for the first time alongside Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , arguing too many people are giving former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  a pass.\par \par \uc2 FORMER FIRST LADY \uc2 MICHELLE OBAMA\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I hope that you'll forgive me if I'm a little angry that we are indifferent to his erratic behavior, his obvious mental decline, his history as a convicted felon.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But it was her powerful turn to the fight over powerful turn to the fight over reproductive rights that set her speech apart. The former first lady laying bare real-life consequences of the strict, new anti-abortion laws put in place since the fall of Roe v. Wade. Talking about women's health in detail. Doctors unsure if they can treat miscarriages, that clinics that provide breast cancer screenings will close, or that there will be fewer OBGYNs. She also directed remarks to men, saying a vote for Trump was a vote against women's health.\par \par \uc2 FORMER FIRST LADY \uc2 MICHELLE OBAMA\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 If we don't get this election right, your wife, your daughter, your mother, we as women will become collateral damage to your rage.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Harris too zeroing in on another issue that affects women deeply in the country, caring for seniors and the elderly, talking about one of her campaign proposals to have Medicare cover the cost of home health care.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 It's about their dignity, but we have a lot of people right now living in what we call the sandwich generation, who are taking care of your kids while you're taking care of your you're taking care of your parents.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With early voting kicking off in the state this weekend, the former president also in Michigan.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP STOPS IN MICHIGAN WITH LOCAL MUSLIM LEADERS WHO HAVE ENDORSED HIM\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We have a chance, but Michigan, we win Michigan, we win the whole deal.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Inviting local Arab and Muslim leaders who've endorsed him on stage.\par \par \uc2 LOCAL MUSLIM LEADER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Because he promises peace.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump has promised, if elected, to reinstate the so-called Muslim ban to keep Muslims from entering the country. During his first term, he also cut off US aid to Palestine, but he predicted Harris would lose Arab American votes over the war in Gaza.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 She would get us into World War III because she's too grossly incompetent to do anything about it.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) He capped his day campaigning at \uc2 Penn State University\uc2 , zeroing in on students in the crowd and transgender athlete.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FMR PRES ZEROES IN ON STUDENTS & TRANS ATHLETES AT PENN STATE UNIVERSITY\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Our country has really gotten bad. It's gotten bad. It's so sad. When you look at the things we're doing, that we even have to say, like, men playing in women's sports. I don't think so.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, Harris today heads to Pennsylvania too as Trump holds that rally in New York City, a kickoff to his closing arguments. Yesterday, he called into an event with the New York State Republican Party. He called New York City a deteriorating city, and he said all the rich people are leaving. Janai?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A lot to be watched for tonight. Maryalice Parks, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241031ekar0005n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HELPING WOMEN THRIVE DURING MENOPAUSE DR. JESSICA SHEPHERD TALKS NEW BOOK "GENERATION M"\b0\par\par\uc2 744 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 12 DAYS TO GO\par \par \uc2 2024, HARRIS, VOTERS, WALZ, KELLY, TRUMP, FASCIST, HITLER, MUSK, BACON, OSBORN\par \par \uc2 ARIZONA, KELLY, SHOOTINGS, CYBERATTACK, GEORGIA, VOTER, WEBSITE\par \par \uc2 WAR, UKRAINE, PUTIN, RUSSIA, KOREA, SOLDIERS, AUSTIN, KIRBY\par \par \uc2 BOEING, CONTRACT, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SATELLITE & RADAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NY LIBERTY VICTORY PARADE\par \par \uc2 MUSIC VIDEO CLIP FROM TAYLOR SWIFT\par \par \uc2 E. COLI, \uc2 MCDONALD'S\uc2 , QP, LAWSUIT, WASHINGTON, TAYLOR FARMS, ONIONS, ERLENGER\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, TRIAL, RESENTENCING, GASC\u211\'00\'D3N, VANDERMOLEN\par \par \uc2 PAYNE, ONE DIRECTION, HOTEL, DEATH, CASSIDY, BYRNE, "X FACTOR", DRUGS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 WNBA, \uc2 LIBERTY\uc2 , VICTORY, PARADE, LYNX, KNICKS TAPE, CONFETTI, ELLIE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE TO THE FINISH LINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 12 DAYS TO GO\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, KELLY, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 HOUSING MARKET\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SHOPPING, PRICES, SAVINGS\par \par \uc2 "MUSIC BY JOHN WILLIAMS", BURNETT, MCELHENNEY\par \par \uc2 SWIFT, MACK, FRIENDSHIP BRACELETS\par \par \uc2 SHOPPING, DEALS, DISCOUNT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEALS & STEALS WITH TORY JOHNSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 EPHRON, MARGULIES, GALLAGHER, "LEFT ON TENTH"\par \par \uc2 GREENBERG, LEWIS, "\uc2 JOHN LEWIS\uc2 : A LIFE"\par \par \uc2 SHEPHERD, MENOPAUSE, "GENERATION M"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELPING WOMEN THRIVE DURING MENOPAUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DR. JESSICA SHEPHERD TALKS NEW BOOK "GENERATION M"\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We turn to a new book that aims to serve as a guide for women as they go through menopause. Dr. Jessica Shepherd offers a new plan living in "Generation M: Living Well in Perimenopause and Menopause."\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM TV SHOW, "SEX AND THE CITY"\par \par \uc2 KIM CATTRALL (ACTRESS)\par \par \uc2 I am leading the way through the menopause maze.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It's a fact of life, all women will experience menopause. But many don't know what that really means, how it will change them, and what to expect.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (AUTHOR "GENERATION M")\par \par \uc2 The topic is something that is often seen as taboo or stigmatized. And even for health care providers, there wasn't a lot devoted towards educating doctors on menopause. And you really owe it to women to be able to educate them in the best ways.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In her new book, "Generation M: Living Well in Perimenopause and Menopause," Dr. Jessica Shepherd, a board-certified OBGYN and women's health advocate, aims to help women thrive during this transition.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (AUTHOR "GENERATION M")\par \par \uc2 The goal of this book is to have knowledge and education towards what is going to be best for me? What are the things I can implement into my life? What are the things that I would want to ask my doctor? And how can I share my experiences with others?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOP COMPLAINTS DURING PERIMENOPAUSE & MENOPAUSE\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Dr. Shepherd says, pay attention to your symptoms. The top complaints and concerns she hears from women are hot flashes, night sweats, mood changes, and sleep disturbances.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (AUTHOR "GENERATION M")\par \par \uc2 There can actually be long-term outcomes that can come from menopause and the decline in estrogen. And those things include decrease in muscle mass, osteoporosis, and decrease in our bone mineral density. But also, heart disease and Alzheimer's disease.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) So, the practical guidebook serves as a tool, even encouraging a holistic approach to empower women.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (AUTHOR "GENERATION M")\par \par \uc2 So, that can be with your diet and changing how you fuel your body, your exercise regimen, and making sure that you're improving muscle mass.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The book also diving into the topic of hormone replacement therapy.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (AUTHOR "GENERATION M")\par \par \uc2 One of the biggest misconceptions during this timeframe is hormones and are they good for you? Are they safe? And "Generation M" really focuses a lot on the ABCs of HRT.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Ultimately, she says the key is finding a community and knowing you are not alone in this journey.\par \par \uc2 DR JESSICA SHEPHERD (AUTHOR "GENERATION M")\par \par \uc2 I wrote "Generation M" as a love letter to all women, so that they can know that they're not alone, but also not to be afraid of what's coming in the future and to give themselves the best tools, so that they can feel themselves and stronger and better as we start to age.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) "Generation M: Living Well in Perimenopause and Menopause" is available right now. Coming up, the cast of the Broadway show, "A Wonderful World: The Louis Armstrong Musical" performs live on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241105ekao0003h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEIGHT LOSS MEDICATION & MENOPAUSE HOW THEY CAN HELP & THE POTENTIAL RISKS\b0\par\par\uc2 709 \uc2 words\par \uc2 23 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP BLASTED BY FORMER CHIEF OF STAFF\par \par \uc2 KELLY, TRUMP, "NYT", FASCIST, HITLER, CHARACTER\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, MEDIA, ELECTION, TRUMP, OBAMA, CAMPAIGN\par \par \uc2 KELLY, TRUMP, FASCIST, CRITIQUES, ADMINISTRATION\par \par \uc2 US TROOPS, \uc2 ISIS\uc2 , INJURED, RAID\par \par \uc2 E. COLI, DEAD, SICKNESS, \uc2 MCDONALD'S\uc2 , CDC\par \par \uc2 NBA\uc2 , LAKERS, LEBRON, BRONNY, HISTORY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRE DANGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DELPHI, MURDERS, TRIAL, EVIDENCE, WILLIAMS, GERMAN\par \par \uc2 GIULIANI, MOSS, FREEMAN, JUDGMENT, DEFAMATION, POSSESSIONS\par \par \uc2 VALENZUELA, DODGERS, WORLD SERIES, CY YOUNG, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 JEFFRIES, SEX TRAFFICKING, ABERCROMBIE, PEACE, DENNEHY, PAUL\par \par \uc2 AMERICAN AIRLINES, BOARDING, TECHNOLOGY, PASSENGERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOMORROW MORNING\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , KELLY\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 MCDONALD'S\uc2 , E. COLI\par \par \uc2 OCTOBER, SELF IMPROVEMENT\par \par \uc2 WEIGHT, MEDICATION, MENOPAUSE, MOONEY, COCKRELL\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the effects of weight loss medications on menopause. Erielle Reshef is back with a look at how losing weight could help curb other symptoms. Good morning to you, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WEIGHT LOSS MEDICATION & MENOPAUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW THEY CAN HELP & THE POTENTIAL RISKS\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, Robin. More and more women are speaking openly about menopause and the changes that this phase of life can bring. Now doctors say GLP-1 medications like Ozempic and Wegovy can be helpful for some patients in curbing the dreaded menopausal weight gain.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Every woman goes through it, the change. Menopause can come with stigma and body changes like weight gain.\par \par \uc2 YOKASTA MOONEY (USED WEIGHT LOSS MEDICATION DURING MENOPAUSE)\par \par \uc2 We feel like it's our fault. We feel like, what did I do wrong? Think, like, our bodies are turning against us.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At age 54, Yokasta Mooney says the scale hit the highest number she'd ever seen.\par \par \uc2 YOKASTA MOONEY (USED WEIGHT LOSS MEDICATION DURING MENOPAUSE)\par \par \uc2 At this point, I don't fit into any of my clothes. All my pictures are from here up, they're cropped. No pictures from below. I was desperate at this point.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Shifts in hormones make it a challenge for menopausal women to lose weight. And more and more doctors are turning to Mounjaro and other weight loss drugs to help. But they are not without risks. Experts warn these medications may exacerbate the loss of muscle mass and bone density already common among menopausal women.\par \par \uc2 DR. LISA SHEPHERD (AUTHOR OF "GENERATION M" & OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 As we start to age our bones are going to be weaker and we're going to lose muscle mass, which is going to increase your risk for things such as osteoporosis and even falls.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The good news? You can keep muscle and bone loss at bay through a proper diet and exercise.\par \par \uc2 DR. LISA SHEPHERD (AUTHOR OF "GENERATION M" & OBGYN)\par \par \uc2 With diet, you significantly want to increase your protein intake. And then exercise, changing those regimens to more of resistance training and weight lifting.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Yokasta lost 30 pounds on Ozempic and was able to lose the next 30 on her own.\par \par \uc2 YOKASTA MOONEY (USED WEIGHT LOSS MEDICATION DURING MENOPAUSE)\par \par \uc2 I was keeping up a journal. I was exercising. I realized throughout that process we think that we eat a lot less than what we really eat.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) An added bonus, doctors say weight loss can help with the severity of other menopause symptoms like hot flashes and night sweats. 56-year-old Lisa Cockrell who lost 20 pounds on Mounjaro says her outlook on managing menopause has changed for the better.\par \par \uc2 LISA COCKRELL (USED WEIGHT LOSS MEDICATION DURING MENOPAUSE)\par \par \uc2 I feel like this stage of life and this journey is totally, totally doable. That we can go through menopause and we can go through this journey and actually have a full life and live in wellness.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is giving women so much hope. Experts say that there's no shame in talking to your doctor about whether medication used for weight loss is right for you. Just be sure that you are getting these drugs through a prescription from a reputable licensed practitioner. Guys?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That is key right there. All right, Erielle, thanks so much.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241105ekan0000l\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 STOCKING UP ON PANTRY ESSENTIALS STAPLES THAT HELP REDUCE RISK OF BREAST CANCER\b0\par\par\uc2 1,161 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ELECTION INTERFERENCE\par \par \uc2 MIDDLE EAST, WAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , SINWAR\par \par \uc2 ALLEN, TRIAL, MURDER\par \par \uc2 AMERICAN AIRLINES, CESSNA\par \par \uc2 COAST GUARD, RESCUE, PACIFIC OCEAN, KAWAI, KEAULANA\par \par \uc2 ONE DIRECTION, INVESTIGATION, PAYNE\par \par \uc2 LYNX, WNBA\par \par \uc2 ELECTION\par \par \uc2 "COLLEGE GAMEDAY", COLLEGE FOOTBALL\par \par \uc2 FLORIDA, MILTON, AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, CAMPAIGN, ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE: SPRING TO THE FINISH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP HARRIS SHARPENS ATTACKS AGAINST TRUMP\par \par \uc2 ATTACK, ROCKET, DRONE, ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , IRON DOME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HEZBOLLAH ESCALATES ATTACKS ON ISRAEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LAUNCHING ROCKEST & DRONES, IRON DOME INTERCEPTING\par \par \uc2 FORMULA ONE, FOOTBALL, AUSTIN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS TAKEOVER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FOOTBALL & F1 EVENTS DOMINATING AUSTIN THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 "THE CATFISHING OF TEGAN AND SARA", DOCUMENTARY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOING INSIDE "THE CATFISHING OF TEGAN AND SARA"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INDIE POP DUO ENDURING DECADE-LONG ONLINE SCHEME\par \par \uc2 LYNX, LIBERTY, WNBA, GAME FIVE, DUNCAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL EYES ON THE WNBA FINALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LYNX FORCE GAME 5 AGAINST NY LIBERTY\par \par \uc2 SOLIDIFIER, TOWELS, SPATULAS, DRINKWARE, COOKIES, MIXES\par \par \uc2 VIDEO, PREGNANCY, ANNOUNCEMENT\par \par \uc2 FIRE, OBESITY, JACKMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRE WEATHER ALERTS\par \par \uc2 SPRINGSTEEN, MUSIC, THE BOSS, "ROAD DIARY"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "BACKSTAGE AND BACKSTREETS" WITH THE BOSS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRUCE SPRINGSTEEN OPENS UP ABOUT MAKING MUSIC\par \par \uc2 COOKING, FOOD, BELLER, BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STOCKING UP ON PANTRY ESSENTIALS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STAPLES THAT HELP REDUCE RISK OF BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) we are back now with our series "Power in Pink" for Breast Cancer Awareness Month and the five pantry go-tos that could help lower your risk of breast cancer and support your overall health. Dietician \uc2 Rachel Beller\uc2  is here. She's the bestselling author of "SpiceRack." Thank you so much for being with us, Rachel. So, it's important to note that no single food or diet can prevent or cure cancer, but these all pack a nutritional punch.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Yes, and I'm glad you mentioned that, very important to note that no single food or diet can prevent or cure cancer, but what we eat over time collectively could make a difference.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEHYDRATED MUSHROOMS\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, all right, important to know. So, first up, I haven't gotten into mushrooms, dehydrated mushrooms. Tell me about them.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 So, we're talking about our power pantry and, of course, fresh mushrooms are incredible, but in our power pantry, we can keep dry, dehydrated mushrooms so we can always have them on hand. And when it comes to breast cancer risk reduction, I love these because they're rich in aromatase inhibitors, which support reducing\u160\'00\'A0breast cancer risk. And it's so easy. You always have it on hand, which is great. They're also rich in beta glucans, which is a soluble fiber that supports our gut health, which supports our immune function. So, really good there, and they're budget friendly. You always have them around. You can get all kinds of different mushrooms.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 And then people ask me, "What do you do with this?" So, you cook it like you would pasta, just longer, about 30 minutes, strain it, and then you can saute it, you're good to go.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really? Okay, I'm glad, right, yeah, oh, okay, yeah, the studio thinks that sounds great.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Totally doable, which is great.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, moving on to flax, ground flax and sesame seeds.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPROUTED OATS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Yes, but before we do that, oats also are rich in beta glucans, which is incredible.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) See, I wasn't sure if you were saying you were going to put those in the oats or what it is. Okay, so overground oats or just regular oatmeal, too, right?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Yes, yes, if you see the sprouted, it enhances the nutrient absorption, but it's not a must, just a little pro tip. But they're also rich in beta glucans, supports our immune function, our gut microbiome.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So the beta glucans, those are good things.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Really good things, special fibers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROUND FLAX, SESAME SEEDS & TAHINI PASTE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, now we are going to go to the ground flax sesame seed.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Yes, so these foods, ground flax, sesame seeds, are rich in lignans. Flax seeds have lignans, and those support our hormonal balance, which is important when it comes to reducing breast cancer risk. Also, if you spot the sprouted ground, grab them. The cost difference isn't, it's not that much but really great because it also enables us to absorb more of those important nutrients, as well.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, you're saying if you can find it and ground it up at home yourself...\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Yes, it should be ground, and if you see it sprouted, great. If not, it's still great. Sesame seeds, second highest source of lignans.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Yes, amazing, and you can just sprinkle that on a salad.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sesame sees are good and very versatile.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Really good, and they're so flavorful. And then you have tahini paste. You can also make a dip out of that. And, of course, I spice everything, hence "SpiceRack," so I've got my super sumac here that you can further elevate the nutritional power. And we have all this with the book.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm glad you said that because we're running out of time. So, real quick, I want to get to a juice. You said always keep a drink on hand.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CITRUS MATCHA TONIC\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Yes, so this is matcha, rich in EGCG, powerful antioxidants. This is meant to stay. Matcha is here to stay. A lot of research points to breast health.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Comes to stay.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Yes, so this is great. One little tip, if you add a little bit of citrus into your matcha, your body will absorb more of those EGCGs. So, that's a good tip right there.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good to know, and then just real quick keeping fiber around also is going to be good for you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIBER BOOSTERS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 Fiber boosters are important, basil seeds, whole hemp, chia seeds. You really want to crank up that fiber to help reduce breast cancer risk. So, this is an easy way to do it. You could add these fiber boosters to salsa, to guac, to quinoa, anything. And again, we have all of this at bellernutrition.com, all packaged for you, easy.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And just good, nutritional punch for you. Thank you so much, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL BELLER\uc2  ("SPICERACK")\par \par \uc2 So great to be here.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241101ekaj0000s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HARRIS ON BATTLEGROUND BLITZ VICE PRESIDENT CRISSCROSSES WISCONSIN IN EFFORT TO SHORE UP "BLUE WALL"\b0\par\par\uc2 686 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 HAMAS\uc2  LEADER KILLED\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , SINWAR, NETANYAHU, GAZA, SIEGEL\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, SINWAR, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , HOSTAGES, DEATH\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, GAZA, ISRAEL, SINWAR, ALLIES, HONOR\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, CAMPAIGN, BLUE WALL, RALLY, ABORTION, JAN 6TH\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, big agendas right there. Selina, thank you so much for that. And Vice President Harris also hopeful that, quote, "This moment gives us an opportunity to finally end the war in Gaza." This comes as Harris is aiming to shore up the so-called blue wall in a race for the White House. And we're tracking both campaigns. Rachel Scott is standing by with the latest on Trump, but first chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce is in Wisconsin tracking Harris. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS ON BATTLEGROUND BLITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VICE PRESIDENT CRISSCROSSES WISCONSIN IN EFFORT TO SHORE UP "BLUE WALL"\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Michael. Well as we head into this final sprint now, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is really upping the pace and intensity of her campaigning and the intensity of her warnings about a Trump second term. Overnight with a blistering rebuke of his position on abortion.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, with abortion front and center in this race, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  taking \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to task for his shifting position.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS ON BATTLEGROUND BLITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP TAKES TRUMP TO TASK FOR HIS SHIFTING POSITION ON ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Now \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has a very different view on reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) During a rally in Green Bay, Wisconsin, Harris letting Trump speak for himself.\par \par \uc2 FMR PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 For 54 years they were trying to get Roe V. Wade terminated, and I did it.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 No, Donald, everybody did not want Roe V. Wade to be overturned. Women are dying of sepsis because they cannot get the health care they need. They did not want this.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Harris calling Trump out for trying to soften his stance on abortion after he told a town hall of all women voters this week that he's the, quote, "Father of IVF."\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 And now the man calls himself the father of IVF. I mean, what does that even mean? He is the one, by the way, who is responsible for it being at risk in the first place.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Harris upping her warnings about a second Trump term, hammering the message that he is a danger to democracy, going after Trump's suggestion that he would use the military to go after his opponents.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Journalists whose stories he doesn't like. Nonpartisan election officials who refuse to cheat by finding a few extra votes for him. Judges who insist on following the law instead of following him. It is for reasons like these that General \uc2 Mark Milley\uc2 , the former chairman of the joint chiefs of staff, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's top general, has called Trump, and I quote, "Fascist to the core."\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And slamming him for calling January 6th a, quote, "Day of love."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS ON BATTLEGROUND BLITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP BLASTS TRUMP FOR SAYING JANUARY 6TH WAS "DAY OF LOVE"\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 140 law enforcement officers were injured that day. Law enforcement officers were killed that day. And what did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  say last night about January 6th? He called it, quote, "A day of love." And we are all clear the American people are exhausted with his gas lighting. Exhausted. Enough. Enough.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Harris now heads to Michigan today with several events there as she tries to shore up support in the rust belt, those key blue wall state. She's been in Georgia this weekend. And next week she's bringing out her heavy hitters, appearing for the first time on the trail alongside the Obamas. Whit.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241031ekai0002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE HEATS UP HARRIS PRESSES APPEAL TO REPUBLICAN VOTERS AS TRUMP AIMS TO WIN OVER WOMEN\b0\par\par\uc2 1,742 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 19 DAYS TO GO\par \par \uc2 RACE, HARRIS, TRUMP, FOX, BIDEN, IMMIGRATION, JAN. 6, RIOT, GONZ\u192\'00\'C0LEZ, VOTERS, IVF, 538\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And we're gonna begin, though, with the race for the White House. Just 19 days until the final votes. Vice President Harris aiming to win over Republican voters while former President Trump aiming to boost his support among women. Our chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce starts us off in Philadelphia. Good morning to you, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE HEATS UP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS PRESSES APPEAL TO REPUBLICAN VOTERS AS TRUMP AIMS TO WIN OVER WOMEN\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. Yeah, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  overnight in some unfamiliar territory, her first interview with Fox News as she tries to win over Republicans. And this was contentious. She was pressed on her record, on the economy, on immigration and on many of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's attack lines. But Harris pushed back, trying to cast her as the candidate of change and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as a danger to democracy.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The interview heated from the start.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM FOX NEWS INTERVIEW\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 And, and so, but...\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 It was essentially, pathway to citizenship for the...\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 May I please finish...\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yes, ma'am.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 May I finish, may I finish responding, please?\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 But here, but this...\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 But you have to let me finish, please.\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You had the...\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After struggling in recent days to show she would govern differently from President Biden, the Vice President trying to put a clear distance between herself and the administration she still serves in but not pinpointing any major policy shifts.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Let me be very clear, my presidency will not be a continuation of \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's presidency. And, like every new president that comes in to office, I will bring my life experiences, my professional experiences and fresh and new ideas.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fox's Bret Baier pushing Harris on the administration's record on immigration.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS PRESSES APPEAL TO REPUBLICAN VOTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP SITS DOWN FOR FOX INTERVIEW, CAMPAIGNS WITH GOP SUPPORTERS\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How many illegal immigrants would you estimate your administration has released into the country over the last three and a half years?\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, I'm glad you raised the issue of immigration because I agree with you, it is a, it is a, a topic of discussion that people want to rightly have. And you know what I'm gonna talk about right now, which is...\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, but do you, just a number, do you think it's one million, three million?\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 But, but, Bret, let's just get to the point. Okay? The point is that we have a broken immigration system that needs to be repaired. And...\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 So your Homeland Security Secretary said that 85 percent of apprehensions...\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Well, I'm not, but I'm not finished. We have a, we have an immigration system that needs to be (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 A rough estimate of six million people have been released.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Speaking to an audience traditionally of Trump supporters, Harris blasting the former president as unstable and dangerous, calling Trump out for increasingly threatening his political opponents, and what he calls the enemy from within.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 And you and I both know that he's talked about turning the American military on the American people. He has talked about going after people who are engaged in peaceful protest. He's talked about locking people up because they disagree with him. This is a democracy. And in, in a democracy, the President of the United States, in the United States of America, should be willing to be able to handle criticism without saying he'd lock people up for doing it. And this is what is at stake.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Harris is now in Wisconsin today with several events on college campuses in that critical state. She then heads, heads to Michigan tomorrow and then Georgia over the weekend, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Mary, thanks very much. Rachel Scott is here with the latest on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . No matter what the planned subject is that day, it always comes back to January 6th.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP PUSHES FALSE JAN 6TH CLAIMS AT TOWN HALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SAYS SUPPORTERS "DIDN'T COME BECAUSE OF ME. THEY CAME BECAUSE OF THE ELECTION"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It always comes back to January 6th, George. And in these two back-to-back town halls that the former President did, he's trying to appeal to new voters, but instead, he is on defense about his record on abortion rights and also about January 6th.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, appearing at a town hall in South Florida, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  doubling down on his anti-immigrant rhetoric and continuing to push false claims about the 2020 Election. The former president taking a question from a Republican voter who says he no longer is supporting him because of his actions on January 6th.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM JANUARY 6\par \par \uc2 RAMIRO GONZ\u192\'00\'C0LEZ (FLORIDA VOTER)\par \par \uc2 (inaudible) Trump. Good evening, Mr. Trump. Okay. I am a Republican, no longer registered though. I want to give you the opportunity to try to win back my vote, okay. Your, I'd say action and maybe inaction during your presidency and the last few years, sort of, you know, was a little disturbing to me. You know, what happened during January 6th and the fact that, you know, you waited so long to take action while your supporters were attacking the Capitol.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump responding by claiming the January 6th attack was a day of love, denying his supporters came at his behest.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 They didn't come because of me. They came because of the election. They thought the election was a rigged election. And that's why they came.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VANCE BACKS TRUMP'S FALSE ELECTION CLAIMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUNNING MATE SAYS FORMER PRESIDENT DID NOT LOSE 2020 RACE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The reality, Trump urged his supporters to travel to Washington promising it will be wild. He waited for hours to call off the mob. More than 140 police officers were assaulted by rioters. He's vowed to pardon those who have been convicted. His running mate, Senator JD Vance now openly agreeing with Trump's demonstrably false claim that he didn't lose the 2020 Election, after not directly answering questions about election integrity for weeks. And in an out-push to appeal to women voters, Trump attending a Fox News town hall with only women in the audience, declaring himself the, quote, "father of IVF."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP AIMS TO WIN OVER WOMEN VOTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT DECLARES HIMSELF "THE FATHER OF IVF"\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Oh, I want to talk about IVF. I'm the father of...\par \par \uc2 HARRIS FAULKNER (FOX NEWS)\par \par \uc2 You don't hear that every day.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'm the father of IVF.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ADDRESSES ABORTION & IVF ISSUES AT ALL-WOMEN TOWN HALL\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The former president asked to address concerns about the growing number of state abortion bans imposed after he appointed three of the Supreme Court justices who supported overturning Roe versus Wade. That decision putting IVF at risk in some state, too. Nowhere more so than Alabama, whose Republican-dominated State Supreme Court ruled embryos used in IVF are children, halting the procedure for weeks.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I got a call from Katy Brick, a young, just a fantastically attractive person from Alabama. She's a senator. And she called me up, like, "emergency, emergency." And I said explain IVS very, IVF very quickly. And within about two minutes I understood it. I said, "No, no, we are totally in favor of IVF."\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  seizing on that moment.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I found it to be quite bizarre, actually. He called himself the father of IVF. And if what he meant is taking responsibility, well then, yeah, he should take responsibility for the fact that one-in-three women in America live in a Trump abortion ban state.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF THE RACE WITH 19 DAYS TO GO\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW POLLS IN TWO KEY BATTLEGROUNDS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, out on the campaign trail \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  often boasts and brags about appointing three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe verses Wade. Now he's aware, George, this all could be a political liability for him because he is behind with likely female voters.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. And meantime, you do have some new polling from battleground states?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC NEWS/YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 538, GEORGIA POLLING AVERAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NORTH CAROLINA POLLING AVERAGE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. And so, 47 states have already started early voting including two critical battlegrounds this week, including the state of Georgia. And so, our friends at FiveThirtyEight had crunched the numbers. Just look how tight this race is, less than two points separating Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  from former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Remember he lost this state by a razor-thin margin, just over 11,000 votes back in 2020. And then, of course, today in the critical battleground of North Carolina, early voting begins here today as well. And this one even tighter, less than a point separating these two candidates. And nationally, George, this race still a dead heat, closer than ever.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sure is. Okay, Rachel, thanks very much. Michael?\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241031ekah00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 IUDS & BREAST CANCER RISK STUDY: HORMONAL IUDS MAY SLIGHTLY RAISE THE RISK FOR WOMEN\b0\par\par\uc2 550 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 19 DAYS TO GO\par \par \uc2 RACE, HARRIS, TRUMP, FOX, BIDEN, IMMIGRATION, JAN. 6, RIOT, GONZ\u192\'00\'C0LEZ, VOTERS, IVF, 538\par \par \uc2 PAYNE, ONE DIRECTION, FALL, HOTEL, ARG., 911, FANS, "STORY OF MY LIFE", CASSIDY, SON\par \par \uc2 CHURCH, ABUSE, SETTLEMENT, ARCHDIOCESE, GOMEZ\par \par \uc2 US, BOMBERS, HOUTHIS, YEMEN, ISRAEL, LEBANON, NETANYAHU, IRAN, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 WORLD SERIES, DODGERS, OHTANI, METS, TAYLOR, LINDOR, \uc2 YANKEES\uc2 , GUARDIANS\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM WNBA\par \par \uc2 PAYNE, ONE DIRECTION, "X FACTOR", "BEAUTIFUL", HENRY, STYLES, HEALTH, ALBUM\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, SENTENCING, VANDERMOLEN, LA, GASCON, BARALT, ANDERSEN\par \par \uc2 "DIDDY", LAWSUIT, ACCUSERS, PARHAM, SHAKUR\par \par \uc2 STUDY, OZEMPIC, WEGOVY, INTOXICATION, OVERDOSE, WIDMER, MARTIN\par \par \uc2 WNBA, LIBERTY, STEWART, IONESCU, LINX\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 SECRET SERVICE, ASSASSINATION ATTEMPT, ROWE\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY GIFTS, SHIPPING DATES\par \par \uc2 HORMONAL IUD, BREAST CANCER, RISK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now a new study about a possible link between certain IUDs and increased breast cancer risk. Eva Pilgrim joins us now with those details. Good morning, Eva.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IUDS & BREAST CANCER RISK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STUDY: HORMONAL IUDS MAY SLIGHTLY RAISE THE RISK FOR WOMEN\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, Robin. Hormonal IUDs may slightly raise your risk of breast cancer. It is a surprising discovery out of a new study. Researchers followed some 79,000 women in Denmark for more than six years.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) What the researchers found is the breast cancer risk with hormonal IUDs is actually about the same as with hormonal pills.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HORMONAL IUD STUDY\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This was an unexpected finding because it was long thought IUDs were lower risk than the pill because lower levels of the hormones were directly released into the uterus. It's important to note, while there is an increased risk, health experts say it is very low. But bottom line here, talk to your doctor about what form of contraception is best for you. It is not a one size fits all. There are a lot of factors to consider when choosing, you guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Eva, thanks very much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GMA MORNING MENU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:13, BACKSTAGE WITH THE BOSS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Coming up in our "GMA Morning Menu," I'll take you behind the scenes with Bruce Springsteen as he gets ready to take the stage. The legendary rocker reflects on everything from career, to fatherhood, to wife and (inaudible) cancer battle.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:41, "GOOD HOUSEKEEPING" TOY AWARDS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Also ahead, we're in the "GMA" Toy Lab with the winners of the 17th Annual Good Housekeeping Toy Awards. There are picks for kids from preschool to tweens.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:20, DEALS & STEALS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, Tory is back with her "Deals & Steals" fall festival. This morning, skincare and beauty must haves starting at less than $5.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 8:24, FLORIDA STRONG\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And "GMA" Florida Strong. Ginger and Victor are there on the ground for us in Tampa with those impacted by the deadly hurricanes. And these folks have no idea they're about to get more than $1 million in help from some wonderful organizations. You do not want to miss what we have in store, so come on back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241031ekah0000h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JUDGE ORDERS 11TH-HOUR DELAY OF EXECUTION SHAKEN BABY SYNDROME CONVICTION DRAWS SCRUTINY\b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , WAR, SINWAR, NETANYAHU, BIDEN, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION, GONZALEZ, JANUARY 6TH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ALL-OUT SPRINT TO ELECTION DAY\par \par \uc2 PAYNE, FALL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHILLING NEW DETAILS IN PAYNE TRAGEDY\par \par \uc2 ROBERSON, WHARTON, SHAKEN BABY SYNDROME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE ORDERS 11TH-HOUR DELAY OF EXECUTION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to the breaking headline from Texas at this hour. Just in, the execution of a prisoner set for 7:00 PM Eastern has suddenly been halted for now. That prisoner on death row, a father convicted of shaken baby syndrome more than 20 years ago. ABC's Mireya Villarreal from Texas.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHAKEN BABY SYNDROME CONVICTION DRAWS SCRUTINY\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, a stunning reprieve just hours before he was set to be put to death. A Texas judge halting the execution of Robert Roberson, the first person scheduled to die by lethal injection in a case of shaken baby syndrome.\par \par \uc2 ROBERT ROBERSON (TEXAS DEATH ROW INMATE)\par \par \uc2 I can't tell you what happened to her because I don't know.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Roberson was convicted of murdering his 2-year-old daughter, Nikki, in 2003. He said he woke to find her unresponsive after she fell off the bed. But a doctor said there were signs of shaken baby syndrome. The detective who helped convict Roberson now believes he is innocent.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN WHARTON (FORMER LEAD DETECTIVE)\par \par \uc2 He's a special man, and I am I'm ashamed that I missed that 20 years ago. We were looking for an offender, and we labeled him as such, and we made it stick all based on junk science.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 American Academy of Pediatrics\uc2  warns about the dangers of shaking infants. But experts have challenged the shaken baby syndrome used in criminal cases from decades ago when the science was less understood. Roberson's lawyers argued new evidence suggests Nikki died of pneumonia made worse by medication. Wharton, who has worked to try to stop the execution, visiting him in prison with "\uc2 The New York Times\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 BRIAN WHARTON (FORMER LEAD DETECTIVE)\par \par \uc2 What do you want to say to me, you know, me and the folks that helped put you here?\par \par \uc2 ROBERT ROBERSON (TEXAS DEATH ROW INMATE)\par \par \uc2 I'd like let you all know, I forgive y'all and stuff. And I just hope, and hope, and pray, pray that we make things right together.\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, all of this comes as a bipartisan group of Texas legislators fought to stop this execution. Now, it is on hold at least until Monday. That's when we've confirmed Roberson will be able to testify in front of a House committee at noontime. But I've spoken with several House representatives late this afternoon, they say, this I highly unprecedented and there are still a lot of lingering questions. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll be tracking it right through next week, of course, with you, Mireya. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIFEPRISTONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW CHALLENGE TO ABORTION PILL\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, with abortion and reproductive right a key issue this presidential election. Tonight, three states are launching a new push to roll back access to the abortion pill nationwide.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Missouri, Kansas, and Idaho are now challenging FDA regulations that ease access to pills, including dispensing by mail, claiming the drug is dangerous and costly. The Supreme Court rejected an earlier version of a lawsuit. The states hope their new case will have a different outcome.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back tonight, a former Olympian on the run tonight., what he's accused of across the US and Canada. The coldest air of the season coming tonight. The freeze and frost warnings in a moment. And we remember a Hollywood great tonight. She was loved.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241021ekah00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 BREAST CANCER THRIVER'S NEW WAY TO SUPPORT OTHERS NONPROFIT GIFT REGISTRY FOR PEOPLE BATTLING CANCER\b0\par\par\uc2 910 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 20 DAYS TO GO\par \par \uc2 CAMPAIGNS, HARRIS, BATTLEGROUNDS, INTERVIEWS, BIPARTISAN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, MICKLETHWAIT, JAN 6TH, PUTIN, RHETORIC\par \par \uc2 RECORD, VOTING, VOTERS, RULING, CERTIFICATION\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, STRIKES, HUMANITARIAN, GAZA, MILLER\par \par \uc2 FAA\uc2 , RUNWAYS, INCURSIONS, AUDIT, ATC\par \par \uc2 STEWART, EMAIL, WNBA, THREATS\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS, \uc2 YANKEES\uc2 , GUARDIANS, METS, DODGERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WATCHING THE TROPICS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, COPLEY, GASCON, GERAGOS, EVIDENCE, RESENTENCING\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, FALL, KITA, WRIGHT, LIFESAVING\par \par \uc2 PANDAS, NATIONAL ZOO CHINA, DC, BAO LI, QING BAO\par \par \uc2 "DWTS", HOUGH, HAYLEY, BRAIN BLEED\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 CEREAL, DYES\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SPENDING\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, FISHEL\par \par \uc2 ROCK AND ROLL, HALL OF FAME, CHER, KENYA, ELEPHANTS, SMITHSONIAN, ZOO, PANDAS\par \par \uc2 DEALS, FALL\par \par \uc2 ALVAREZ, "ENGLISH TEACHER"\par \par \uc2 KALVER, CANCER, WEGOTTHIS\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back now with Power in Pink for breast cancer awareness month. There is a huge community of thrivers who lean on each other for support, and Erielle Reshef has the story of one thriver who came up with a great way to help others through their cancer journeys. Good morning, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER THRIVER'S NEW WAY TO SUPPORT OTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NONPROFIT GIFT REGISTRY FOR PEOPLE BATTLING CANCER\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning to you, Robin. This is truly brilliant. It's an idea born from personal experience. A young mom going through chemo, realizing there's a better way to streamline the flood of good will from friends and family and channel it into things that a patient really needs.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Less than a year after giving birth to her first child, Elissa Kalver was diagnosed with metastatic breast cancer, the cancer spreading to her liver and spine. Alyssa was just 34 years old.\par \par \uc2 ELISSA KALVER (WEGOTTHIS.ORG FOUNDER & CEO)\par \par \uc2 I remember sitting in the doctor's office when they pulled up my PET scan. And that was when my husband went pale and was breathing into a paper bag. I was sitting there in shock.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When the Los Angeles mom started chemo, she was inundated with the well intentioned question from family and friends, what can I do to help?\par \par \uc2 ELISSA KALVER (WEGOTTHIS.ORG FOUNDER & CEO)\par \par \uc2 I really didn't have an answer because I didn't know what I needed and I didn't want to ask for help.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This got Elissa thinking, what if there was something like a wedding registry to take the guess work out of the equation for anyone battling cancer? During her fifth round of chemo, WeGotThis.org was born.\par \par \uc2 ELISSA KALVER (WEGOTTHIS.ORG FOUNDER & CEO)\par \par \uc2 It's the first ever non-profit gift registry for cancer patients. Our mission is to, you know, build a community of giving and receiving that helps people like me live our best lives.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Friends and family can search the website to find a patient's registry and just click to buy the goods or services they requested. And for those going through treatment, there are suggestions for things you may not even know you need.\par \par \uc2 HEATHER BARRY (WEGOTTHIS.ORG PATRON)\par \par \uc2 You can register for sweaters that have zippers on the sides that make it easier for chemotherapy. I had one that was Oscar de la Renta, so I felt kind of, you know, extra wearing that one.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For 35-year-old mom Heather Barry, whose cancer battle started last year, WeGotThis.org was a game changer.\par \par \uc2 HEATHER BARRY (WEGOTTHIS.ORG PATRON)\par \par \uc2 We are able to register for any type of gift card. There are the ability to add pillows, blankets, contribute $20, $100, and it goes straight to you.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Elissa's metastatic breast cancer is incurable, but her outlook is inspiring. She says she prioritizes living, not just staying alive.\par \par \uc2 ELISSA KALVER (WEGOTTHIS.ORG FOUNDER & CEO)\par \par \uc2 People want to help and people need help. And it, having a solution to making this possible in the hard times is like the biggest gift and silver lining out of the worst thing to ever happen to me.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It is really beautiful how she's giving back to her community. And WeGotThis.org registries have been up and running since last summer. So far more than 1,000 registries have been created. Elissa says they have partnered with dozens of organizations and hospitals to get the word out, guys.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, great.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Inspiring.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So smart, right? I mean, you hear, you say, what can I do to help?\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's the instinct.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But, of course, people also don't know what they need sometimes, and this can take the guess work out.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I love it. We got this.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We got this.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, because you want, you, when you're going through it, you're just, are so looking for someone that's, that's got you, and she does. You do always.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's right.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Erielle.\par \par \uc2 ERIELLE RESHEF (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241029ekag0003h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL OPENS UP ABOUT BREAST CANCER DIAGNOSIS "BOY MEETS WORLD" STAR ON HER TREATMENT SO FAR & HER MESSAGE FOR OTHERS\b0\par\par\uc2 866 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 20 DAYS TO GO\par \par \uc2 CAMPAIGNS, HARRIS, BATTLEGROUNDS, INTERVIEWS, BIPARTISAN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, MICKLETHWAIT, JAN 6TH, PUTIN, RHETORIC\par \par \uc2 RECORD, VOTING, VOTERS, RULING, CERTIFICATION\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, STRIKES, HUMANITARIAN, GAZA, MILLER\par \par \uc2 FAA\uc2 , RUNWAYS, INCURSIONS, AUDIT, ATC\par \par \uc2 STEWART, EMAIL, WNBA, THREATS\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS, \uc2 YANKEES\uc2 , GUARDIANS, METS, DODGERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WATCHING THE TROPICS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, COPLEY, GASCON, GERAGOS, EVIDENCE, RESENTENCING\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON, FALL, KITA, WRIGHT, LIFESAVING\par \par \uc2 PANDAS, NATIONAL ZOO CHINA, DC, BAO LI, QING BAO\par \par \uc2 "DWTS", HOUGH, HAYLEY, BRAIN BLEED\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 CEREAL, DYES\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SPENDING\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, FISHEL\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with our "GMA" cover story. "Boy Meets World" actress Danielle Fishel opening up about her breast cancer diagnosis. How her treatment's going so far. Melissa Adan spoke with her. Good morning, Melissa.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. So Danielle Fishel, who is beloved for her role in "Boy Meets World," is now part of the one in three women that are diagnosed with breast cancer each year. I sat down with Danielle and she courageously shared her cancer journey and the tool she credits with saving her life.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning Danielle Fishel, the director, producer, and actress, best known as spunky teen Topanga on the '90s hit "Boy Meets World."\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP OF "BOY MEETS WORLD"\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 No matter how difficult life gets, the important thing is to live it with hope.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Opening up about the diagnosis that changed her world, breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 My doctor told me, you're going to be okay. I just want you to know I'm so thankful that it's stage zero, but I do want you to know there is no easy cancer. And I didn't really quite understood what she meant, but now having, you know, just been on this journey for a couple of months, I get it now.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The 43-year-old mother of two diagnosed with DCIS, ductal carcinoma in situ. Doctors label it stage zero breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 Having to break the news to my husband was really hard. Both of his parents passed from cancer. I waited until the kids went to bed and he actually brought it up. He said, still no results yet, huh? And I said, no, I did get the results back, and do I have cancer. And I, I mean, truly just saw the blood drain from his face.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For the last three months Fishel undergoing two surgery, including a lumpectomy, and weighing her options about treatment.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 My recovery's going well. I no longer have cancer. I do still need to make a decision moving forward about radiation.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She first shared her diagnosis on her podcast, "Pod Meets World" she hosts with "Boy Meets World" costars Rider Strong and Will Friedle.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 I want to share this because I hope that it will encourage anyone to get in there. If it's time for your appointment, if you've never had an appointment before, get in there. I'm so grateful that I prioritized my health and said I'm gonna go and have this mammogram, and it changed my life.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But what was it inside of you that said, no, I have to get this done?\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 As I've gotten older and I've become a mom and wife, and I started thinking, is being selfless actually the virtue we think it is, or is it really harming us? And I think it's really harming us, this idea of putting everybody else before yourself. And when it comes to my health, when it comes to my mental health, those are just two areas I'm not willing to sacrifice for anyone. I'm not willing to be selfless. I'm going to be selfish.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2 , about one in five breast cancers will be DCIS and nearly all women with it can be cured.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 I feel like it's a very Topanga thing to be saying to people, hey, your health matters. Your, your wellness matters. Can you please go have your preventive checkups?\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fishel now using her platform to encourage others to get their mammograms.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 If you grew up watching me on TV it's probably time for you to go have a mammogram, so go get one.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So Topanga-like, and we are so encouraged by her. And Danielle really emphasized that we should not put off getting mammograms, which are recommended starting age 40 or earlier, depending on family history or other risk factors. Guys?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Melissa.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241029ekag0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL "BOY MEETS WORLD" STAR ON HER BREAST CANCER DIAGNOSIS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,197 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Nightline\par \uc2 NLNE\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NIGHTLINE\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, COPLEY, GERAGOS, GASCON, O'DONNELL, VICARY\par \par \uc2 FISHEL, BREAST CANCER, DCIS, "BOY MEETS WORLD"\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Welcome back. She captured viewers' hearts as Topanga on "Boy Meets World." Now, Danielle Fishel shares her breast cancer diagnosis at 43 and how her treatment is going so far. Here's ABC's Melissa Adan.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 I was looking healthy. I was feeling healthy. I didn't have any lump. I was just going about my life.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Actress, director and podcaster Danielle Fishel is opening up about the shock diagnosis she says changed her world.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 And my doctor told me, "You're going to be okay. But I do want you to know there is no easy cancer." And I didn't really quite understood (sic) what she meant but now having, you know, just been on this journey for a couple of months, I get it now.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely, no easy cancer.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 No.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD") (CONTINUED)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She's best known for playing Topanga, a 90s sitcom sweetheart who, as a teen made millions of fans swoon on the hit ABC show "Boy Meets World."\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: "BOY MEETS WORLD"\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 So, what do I tell my mother?\par \par \uc2 BEN SAVAGE ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 Am I your boyfriend?\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 Yes, you are.\par \par \uc2 BEN SAVAGE ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 Then I'll be there.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 You're the best.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This summer, at just 43 years old, Fishel says she was diagnosed with an early form of breast cancer. DCIS, or ductal carcinoma in situ.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Doctors call this kind of cancer stage zero. What was your reaction to that?\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 I had only really been familiar with stages one through four and so stage zero, at first I was, like, does that really make it cancer? But it does.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The married mother of three and five-year-old-boys says she worried how to reveal her diagnosis to her husband and sons.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How has your family been through all of this?\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 Having to break the news to my husband was really hard. He actually brought it up. He said, "Still no results yet, huh?" And I said, "No, I did get the results back and I do have cancer," and I mean, truly, just saw the blood drain from his face. Like, nobody really prepares you for managing the emotions of other people who love you and even though you are the one with the diagnosis, it's really hard to watch your family struggle.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I'm sure at that moment, you're thinking about your kids and so, and how has that conversation been with them?\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 I told them that I was sick and at I was gonna need to have surgery and then that I was gonna be fine.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Danielle Fishel first rocketed to fame on "Boy Meets World."\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: "BOY MEETS WORLD"\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 No matter how difficult life gets, the important thing is to live it with hope.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The coming of age sitcom focused on a group of teens navigating family, school and social dramas. Fishel and her co-star, Ben Savage, even reprising their roles in a reboot, "Girl Meets World."\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP: "GIRL MEETS WORLD"\par \par \uc2 BEN SAVAGE ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 That is the 100th time that you have one, two, three tricked me.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 I do it that often?\par \par \uc2 BEN SAVAGE ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 You've been doing it since the 90s.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fishel now hosts "Pod Meets World," a podcast with two of her "Boy Meets World" costars, Rider Strong and Will Friedle. It's where she first revealed her stage zero diagnosis.\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 I want to share this because I hope that it will encourage anyone to get in there. If it's time for your appointment, if you've never had an appointment before, get in there.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ONE IN FIVE WILL BE DCIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEARLY ALL WOMEN WITH IT CAN BE CURED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SOURCE: AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The America Cancer Society estimates about one in five breast cancers will be DCIS, but nearly all women with it can be cured.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It has just been nearly two months since you revealed the diagnosis. How have you felt since then?\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 I felt great, but honestly, the most important thing to me has been the response that I've had from the amount of people who told me what a difference it's made in their life.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSTAGRAM COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fans showing their support, writing on Fishel's \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , "I'm so glad you caught it early. Getting these screenings is so important," with many others admitting, "Her news influenced me to make an appointment and go." She joins a number of female celebrities going public with their breast cancer diagnoses, from actress Christina Applegate to singer/songwriter Sheryl Crow and even our own robin Roberts back in 2007.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA FOOTAGE FROM 2007\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Extremely grateful that it was found early.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How important was that to you to get your mammogram?\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 It was so important to me. The America Cancer Society recommends that you start getting mammograms at 40, unless you have a family history. And this year, when I got my text saying, "it's time for you to book your appointment," my very first thought was, oh, who has time? Like, I'm so busy and I thought, but don't put it off.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Fishel says she eventually did go and after her diagnosis, is focusing on her future.\par \par \uc2 MELISSA ADAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How is your recovery going?\par \par \uc2 DANIELLE FISHEL ("BOY MEETS WORLD")\par \par \uc2 I no longer have cancer. I do still need to make a decision moving forward about radiation. I don't know what my cancer would've been had I not made my yearly checkup. So, Topanga would want you to do it. I want you to do it. If you grew up watching me on TV, it's probably time for you to go have a mammogram, so go get one.\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our thanks to Melissa.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LIAM PAYNE\par \par \uc2 JUJU CHANG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) When we come back, the shocking death of former One Direction singer Liam Payne. The voice behind huge hits like "The Story Of My Life."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document NLNE000020241021ekag00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 JUST 23 DAYS REMAINING UNTIL 2024 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION TRUMP SPREADS FALSE CLAIMS ABOUT FEDERAL HURRICANE RESPONSE\b0\par\par\uc2 3,312 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2024 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 2024, \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , CAMPAIGN, CLAIMS, VANCE, FEMA, GANGS, ABORTION, AG, 2020\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I'm joined now by Republican vice presidential nominee, Senator JD Vance. So happy to have you here this morning, Senator Vance. I know you've been going hard on the campaign trail, but I want to start with the hurricane. During Hurricane Helene as we heard, former President Trump suggested the federal government was not only sending FEMA aid meant for the hurricane to migrants, but going out of their way to not help people in Republican areas. Do you think that is true?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUST 23 DAYS REMAINING UNTIL 2024 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SPREADS FALSE CLAIMS ABOUT FEDERAL HURRICANE RESPONSE\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, Martha, what the President said is that fundamentally FEMA aid is distracted by going to illegal migrants, and by the way, good morning, and thanks for having me. We've got Republican Congressmen who are on the ground who represent that area saying that they have to call the White House to get food and water to FEMA. I don't frankly think there's anything malicious going on here, Martha, but I do think that we've have had an incompetent response to this particular crisis, particularly in western North Carolina, which to be fair, was hit harder than a lot of us expected it.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 But, fundamentally, if you've got six days after the hurricane, the 82nd Airborne is still trickling in, I do think that we had a fundamentally incompetent, overly bureaucratic response to the hurricane. So, what you hear from folks on the ground is they feel left behind. And Martha, we have to remember, of course, I, I know this area well. This is the Appalachian region of our country where people have felt ignored by their government for 30 years, and it doesn't help when you have a response to the hurricane, that's slow, that's halting, and then you layer on top of it of course, that...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator Vance...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 FEMA has done a lot of immigration resettlement work.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator Vance, I wanna go back to...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Go, go on.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I, I, I wanna go back to what, what former President Trump said. He said, they're going out of their way to not help people in Republican areas. There is no truth to that, and on staging, Pentagon officials say that active duty troops were staged and ready to go before being called upon and were instantly out the door. So, President Trump, former President Trump is saying things that aren't true about that money being withheld from Republican areas.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, Martha, I think you're actually confusing staging of resources from the rapid response of the US military. I mean, look, in FEMA's defense, there are things after this hurricane that FEMA simply could not do. You actually need military command in control. You need military resources deployed to the area. And I think all the President has said is frankly, what - some of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' surrogates have said, which is that if these areas were a little more Democratic, maybe \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  would've focused on them more. That acknowledgment is not to attack frankly the good folks of FEMA. It's to suggest that Americans are feeling left behind by their government, which they are, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. Let's...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 If you talk to folks on the ground, we, we've had, I've had friends who have been in Boone, North Carolina helping with the cleanup, it is an extraordinary sense of betrayal and being left behind. People are worried that their government doesn't care about them. I'm much more worried about the incompetence of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' administration that led to that more than I am...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator Vance, Senator Vance, I'm just gonna say that local officials...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 ...the fact that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  alleges something is, is wrong.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...local officials and FEMA officials say that is just flat wrong. But I wanna, we played some other comments about migrants...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, what, but...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOP MAYOR REFUTES TRUMP CLAIMS OF GANG TAKEOVER IN AURORA\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) (inaudible) ...including in Aurora, in Colorado where Trump said the city had been invaded and conquered by Venezuelan gangs. The Republican mayor of the city said flatly, the city and state have not been taken over or invaded or occupied by migrant gangs. So, do you support \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  making those claims that the Republican mayor says were grossly exaggerated and have hurt the city's identity and sense of safety? I understand what you're saying, that some people left behind, but he's making these statements that the Mayor is flat-out disputing.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, Martha, just said the mayor said they were exaggerated.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Grossly exaggerated.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 That means that there's got to be some, that means there's gotta be some element of truth here, and of course President Trump was actually in Aurora, Colorado talking to people on the ground. And what we're hearing, of course, Martha, is that people are terrified by what has happened with some of these Venezuelan gangs. And (inaudible) conversation, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Sen - Senator Vance, I'm gonna stop you 'cause I know exactly what happened. I'm gonna stop you. The incidents were limited to a handful of apartment conflicts, apartment complexes. And the Mayor said, "Our dedicated police officers have acted on those concerns." A handful of problems.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Only, Martha do you hear yourself? Only a handful of apartment complexes in American were taken over by Venezuelan gangs, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the problem, and not \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' open border? Americans are so fed up with what's going on, and they have every right to be. And I, I really find this exchange, Martha, sort of interesting because you seem to be more focused with nitpicking everything that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has said, rather than acknowledging that apartment complexes in the United States of America are being taken over by violent gangs. I worry so much more about that problem than anything else here.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 We've got to get American communities in a safe space again. And unfortunately, when you let people in by the millions, most of whom are unvetted, most of whom you don't know who they really are, you're going to have problems like this. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , 94 executive orders that undid \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's successful border policies, we knew this stuff would happen.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's, let's...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 They bragged about opening the border, and now we have the consequences and we're living with it. We can do so much better, but frankly, we're not going to do better, Martha, unless \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  calls this stuff out. I'm glad that he did.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. Let's, let's just, let's just end that with they did not invade or take over the city as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  said. I wanna move on to women...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Just a few apartment complexes, no big deal.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) A few apartment complexes that the mayor did not seem was invading the entire city. Let's move on to women and abortion. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is leading \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in our poll among males by eight points, but lagging behind Harris by seven points, nine points among females. You said during the debate that you and Trump have more to do to earn back people's trust, specifically as it relates to women and reproductive rights. Fifty-six percent of those polled support restoring abortion access to what it was under Roe v. way, Roe v. Wade. So what would you say, specifically to the women watching this morning who believe they should have their own say over their bodies, and not the government, either state or federal?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC-IPSOS POLL: HARRIS LEADS WITH WOMEN, TRUMP LEADS WITH MEN\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, Martha, first of all, what I'd say is that I think renationalizing this entire debate is, is a big mistake. And I understand that a lot of Americans according to that poll apparently disagree with me and President Trump here, but we want to respect Californians. We want to respect Alabamans. We want to respect Pennsylvanians. These folks are gonna have different approaches to this particular topic. And I think that what we had in this country for 50 years was a culture war over this particular issue because we had nationalized it.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VANCE AT DEBATE: GOP NEEDS TO EARN PUBLIC'S 'TRUST' BACK ON ABORTION\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 And, and it's also important, Martha, that while \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  uses the slogan of returning to Roe versus Wade, she has endorsed policies that go way beyond anything that Roe versus Wade ever meant in this country. Taxpayer-funded abortions for late-term abortions. She's explicitly refused to endorse things like the Born Alive Act, which would protect babies who survive botched abortions. So, while she hides behind the popular slogan of Roe versus Wade, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' actual abortion views I think are much more radical than even a lot, I think, frankly, most of our pro-choice citizens.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, let, let me go back again. What would you say to those women who don't want people involved in their individual rights? \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is on that side of that, not you.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think that, Martha, that's, that's not right actually. I think \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has taken this so far that a lot of women, if they knew \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' actual view and not the slogan, they would recognize that it's far more radical. They can believe in individual autonomy, but also recognize there are of course, limits here. We don't want to abort nine-month-old babies here and we don't wanna have taxpayers funding it. So, I think everybody recognizes there's a right balance to strike. But to answer your question, Martha, what I would say to women is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I want to make it easier to make the choice of life in the first place.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 And I, I know a lot of young women, especially when I was younger, who chose abortion because they feel like they didn't have any options. And what I want to do as a person who, who, who, admittedly, Martha, wants to protect the most vulnerable members of our society, I'd like to make it easier for women to choose life to begin with. I think that goes to.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Lowering the cost of housing, which, of course, has skyrocketed under \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' administration. I think it's making it easier for working moms to balance work and, and, and life and family. There's a lot that we can do to become more pro-family. That's how I think we can best earn back trust...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 ...and, yes.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator, I want to get to other topics here. On, on the Attorney General.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Sure.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, you said on Friday that the most important person in government in a Trump-Vance administration, other than the President is not you, it would be the Attorney General. Why do you consider that the most important spot, the second most important spot?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VANCE: ATTORNEY GENERAL 2ND MOST IMPORTANT TRUMP ADMIN. ROLE\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Well, one reason, Martha, is just public opinion, and, and what I mean here is that we really want the American people to believe that we have a fair and equitable administration of justice. If not, the entire sort of system falls apart. You need people to believe that if the Attorney General prosecutes somebody, it's motivated by justice and law and not by politics. And unfortunately, what we've seen under \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' leadership.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Would \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  go after his political opponents?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Is the...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Would \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  go after his political opponents?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 No. He...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He's suggested that in the past.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Martha, he was president for four years, and he didn't go after his political opponents. You know who did go after her political opponents? \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , who has tried to arrest everything from pro-life activists to her political opponents and used the Department of Justice...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He said those people who cheated will be prosecuted.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 ...as a weapon against people. Well, he said that people who violated our election laws will be prosecuted. I think that's the administration of law. He didn't say people are gonna go to jail because they disagree with me. That has, in fact, been the administration and the policy of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Martha. Look, over the last three and a half years, we have seen politically motivated after politically motivated prosecution. I'd like us to just get back to a system of law and order, where we try to arrest people when they break the law, not because they disagree with the prevailing opinion of the day.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 And there's a fundamental difference here between \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  may agree, agree or disagree on a particular issue, but he will fight for your right to speak your mind without the government trying to silence you. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has explicitly endorsed censorship of folks who disagree with her.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator Vance, I, I, I, I want to go back to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  again.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 We've got a Department of Justice that believes in the First Amendment, Martha. The First Amendment is the bedrock of our Constitution.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 We have \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  doesn't even believe in it.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Senator, we're just about out of time here.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Go ahead, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're just about out of time here. And I want to end with this, in interview after interview, question after question, and in the debate, you refused to say that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost the 2020 election. So, I'm just gonna assume that if, if I ask you 50 times whether he lost the election, you would not acknowledge that he did. Is that correct?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VANCE REPEATEDLY REFUSES TO ACKNOWLEDGE BIDEN WON IN 2020\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Martha, you've, you, you asked this question. I've been asked this question ten times in the past couple of questions. Of course, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I believe there were problems in 2020. You haven't asked about inflation (inaudible). The American people...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No. I'm sorry. Let's stick to this. I know, I know...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VANCE CONTINUES TO DODGE WHEN ASKED IF TRUMP LOST IN 2020\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 ...want us to talk about how to make their lives better. They don't want us to...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Why won't you say that? Why won't you say that?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Because, because, Martha, I believe that in 2020, when big tech firms were censoring American citizens, that created very serious problems. And by the way, Martha, you're, you're a journalist. You represent the American media. Look at the polling on this. A lot of Americans feel like they were silenced in the runup to the 2020 election. That is such a bigger issue. That fundamental problem...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VANCE PIVOTS TO CENSORSHIP ALLEGATIONS WHEN PRESSED ON 2020 RESULTS\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If, if you, I - just wanna...\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 ...that me and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  talking about it, and unfortunately, Martha, thanks to the fact that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But I don't understand why you won't just say it if you believe it.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 ...she's, what, won't just say what? That I think the 2020 election had some problems? I've said that repeatedly.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Did \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lose? That's the question, and you know that's the question.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Martha, I've said repeatedly I think the 2020 election had problems. You want to say rigged. You want to say he won. Use whatever vocabulary term you want. I want to focus on the fact that we had big technology firms censoring our fellow citizens in a way that violated our fundamental rights. The fact that you're so obsessed with what word I use to describe this phenomenon, rather than the phenomenon itself suggests something very broken in the American media.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 If we want to restore trust in American elections and democracy, which I want to do, Martha, we have to talk openly about what happened in 2020, and most importantly, we've got to talk about what happened afterwards.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 Americans being unable to afford the basic necessities of middle class life.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thank you, Senator Vance.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR JD VANCE (REP-OH) (REPUBLICAN VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 ...because \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is in the White House. Thanks, Martha.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We're gonna leave it right there. Appreciate your time this morning.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Up next, Democratic Governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  on the state of the Harris campaign. We're back in two minutes.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020241023ekad00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 FINISH LINE IN SIGHT: 23 DAYS TO ELECTION DAY VP HARRIS STOPS IN NORTH CAROLINA, RELEASES MEDICAL RECORDS\b0\par\par\uc2 1,171 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPRINT TO THE FINISH\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ELECTION, POLL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FINISH LINE IN SIGHT: 23 DAYS TO ELECTION DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP HARRIS STOPS IN NORTH CAROLINA, RELEASES MEDICAL RECORDS\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we do begin here on your specialty, the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) With just 23 days to go before election day, former President Trump in Arizona today, Vice President Harris in North Carolina. And that is where we find ABC's Maryalice Parks this morning. Good morning, Maryalice.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Gio, good morning. This is the second time Vice President Harris has been to North Carolina since the state was hit hard by Hurricane Helene. The impacts of that storm could be a real wild card in this race. And she made some news yesterday releasing her medical records and calling out former President Trump for not doing the same.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  overnight packing supplies with volunteers in North Carolina for those in the state impacted by Hurricane Helene, and meeting with black community leaders she hopes will rally support for her campaign.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Not yet, my dear.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This weekend, the Vice President also releasing her medical records including details about her allergies, her vision, and her family's medical history, including maternal history for colon cancer.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS MEDICAL RECORDS\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This signed letter from her physician concluding she's in, quote, "excellent health," ending she possesses the physical and mental resilience required to successfully execute the duties of the presidency. Twenty years younger than her opponent, Harris calling out former President Trump for not being as transparent.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 It is clear to me that he and his team do not want the American people to really see what it is that he is doing and whether or not he actually is fit to do the job of being president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Harris pointing out too that he also would not agree to debate her again.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP MEDICAL DIRECTOR\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump's communication director pushing back, writing that he has maintained an extremely busy and active campaign schedule. But his team has not released any medical records recently, not even from the medical team that treated him after the assassination attempt in Pennsylvania in July.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP BARNSTORMS WESTERN STATES, DOUBLES DOWN ON FALSE IMMIGRATION CLAIMS\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump this weekend barnstorming western states with back-to-back events in Nevada and even in Harris' hometown of California overnight. Threatening that, if elected, he would withhold federal disaster aid to the Democratic state unless he adopted policies he liked.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 If you don't do it, we're not giving you any of that fire money that we send you all the time for all the forest fires that you have.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Trump also claimed the country had been invaded. And with increasingly violent language, falsely casted all immigrants as hardened criminals.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Our criminals are considered extremely nice by comparison to the people that we see. They'll cut your throat and, the next morning, they won't even remember. This is what they do.\par \par \uc2 MARYALICE PARKS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, those comments from former President Trump about disaster aid obviously coming as there's been so much conversation about getting relief to those impacted by those back-to-back storms. The White House has been calling Trump out for what it says is spreading false misinformation (sic). I know we're just over three weeks until election day, but early voting has already started in many states, and it starts here in North Carolina on Thursday. Janai?\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, just over three weeks to go. Maryalice, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEY TAKEAWAYS AS NEW POLLS SHOW CANDIDATES IN TIGHT RACE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, part of why it's a joy to have Rachel here is because she is out in the country, all around the country with the campaigns, traveling with them. Rachel, we have a new ABC News-Ipsos poll out this morning. What are some of the key takeaways?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Janai, Gio, this race was close. It is even closer in the final stretch, now just two points separating Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  from former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . Harris still has the edge this race.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: YOUR VOICE, YOUR VOTE 2024\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VOTE PREFERENCE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But when we last did this poll in September, she was ahead by five. So, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  really closing that gap. It is a dead heat in this final stretch. We know that the candidates each have their core issues, right?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , it's immigration. For Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , it is abortion rights. But now, we're getting a snapshot on where voters stand on these issues with just about three weeks to go. So, 56% of Americans now favor deporting all undocumented immigrants.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEPORTATION & ABORTION: DIVERGENT VIEWS\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) That's up 20 points from eight years ago. Trump still leading on immigration. Then on abortion rights, Harris does have the edge on this critical issue. But that same number again, 56% saying the federal government should restore access to abortion to what it was before the Supreme Court overturned Roe versus Wade. And, look, you mentioned, I've been out all across this country.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Pennsylvania, Michigan, Colorado, the number one issue I hear from voters is the economy. And Trump still has the edge on this key issue here. Harris has to make inroads in this final stretch on that.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF THE NATION'S ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that's because it affects everyone, all the families at home when they open their refrigerator, all of those things. Rachel, thank you so much. It is a joy to have you here. And tune into "This Week" later. Martha Raddatz goes one-on-one with Republican vice presidential nominee JD Vance with just 23 days to election day.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS MORNING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATOR JD VANCE, (R) VICE PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOVERNOR \uc2 ANDY BESHEAR\uc2 , (D) KENTUCKY\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Plus, Martha speaks with Kentucky's Democratic Governor \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  about the state of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' campaign. Gio?\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Janai.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241016ekad00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 RISE IN BREAST CANCER IN WOMEN UNDER 50 BREAKING DOWN WHAT'S BEHIND THE ALARMING INCREASE\b0\par\par\uc2 963 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HURRICANE MILTON, AFTERMATH\par \par \uc2 FEMA, MILTON, HELENE\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, TRUMP, HARRIS, IMMIGRATION\par \par \uc2 WAR, MIDDLE EAST, AIRSTRIKES\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS, SEARCH\par \par \uc2 COLORADO, MINE, ACCIDENT, PULSE\par \par \uc2 LOUISVILLE, PLANE CRASH\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL, AL CHAMPIONSHIP, DODGERS\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP OF "FREAKY FRIDAY"\par \par \uc2 "COLLEGE GAMEDAY", COLLEGE FOOTBALL\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, HARRIS, TRUMP, GENDER GAP\par \par \uc2 NATIONAL CHESS DAY, GUNTAKA\par \par \uc2 FREDDIE, FLYING CARPET\par \par \uc2 MILTON, HURRICANE, RESCUE, DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE MILTON'S PATH OF DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OFFICIALS CONTINUE TO RESCUE RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , STRIKES, LEBANON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LEBANON SAYS NEARLY 60 AIRSTRIKES IN PAST 24 HOURS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INCLUDES STRIKES TARGETING CENTRAL BEIRUT\par \par \uc2 WILLIAMS, DANCER, MISSING, BROADWAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT SEARCH FOR MISSING BROADWAY DANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ZELIG WILLIAMS WAS LAST SEEN IN SC ON OCTOBER 3\par \par \uc2 TRAIN, HEIST, MERCHANDISE, INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FREIGHT TRAIN HEIST INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AT LEAST SIX PEOPLE ARRESTED\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, RISK, WOMEN, AGE, MENN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RISE IN BREAST CANCER IN WOMEN UNDER 50\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING DOWN WHAT'S BEHIND THE ALARMING INCREASE\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Back now on "GMA" with our cover story. As, of course, we all know, October is Breast Cancer Awareness Month, and there's been an alarming rise in the number of women under 50 diagnosed with breast cancer in the US. So, here to help us understand what's going on and what women can do is board certified OB/GYN Dr. Corrine Menn. Thank you so much for being here, Dr. Men. Why are these numbers, why are we seeing them going up?\par \par \uc2 DR. INE MENN (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 Well, you know, first of all, I want everyone to know that young women can and do get breast cancer. I'm living proof. I was diagnosed at just 28 years old, and it's actually the most common cancer in women under the age of 40. And, yes, the rates are going up at an alarming rate. We know that women under the age of 50, the rate is increasing by 1.4 percent annually, and in the youngest women in their 20s, the rate's going up by 2.2 percent annually. And, you know, young women have unique challenges. They're diagnosed often at a later stage, a more aggressive cancer, and their diagnosis is often delayed because of their age.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, another important thing to note here is while the numbers of people dying related to breast cancer are going down, we're still seeing some women impacted more than others. Why is that?\par \par \uc2 DR. INE MENN (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 Well, there are racial disparities, and it's really an important point that women of color in particular young, Black women under the age of 35, have double the rate of breast cancer that their white counterparts do. They're also much more likely to be diagnosed with more advanced disease and more aggressive breast cancer, like triple-negative breast cancer. They're less likely to be part of clinical trials, and, really importantly, family history is important for everybody, but Black women are far less likely to be referred to genetic testing based on family history.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so, I check those boxes, and being completely transparent, this is something that is increasingly in the back of my mind. We were just talking off camera about the whole thing around dense breasts, and that can make it more difficult to detect, and women can just, how can we be more proactive about our health? What do we need to know about dense breasts? What questions should we be asking?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S BEHIND SPIKE IN YOUNG WOMEN WITH BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOW TO BE YOUR OWN ADVOVATE & LOWER YOUR RISK RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 DR. INE MENN (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 Yes, well, I think this is a siren call to all women, but especially young women, and I always tell patients you really need to be the CEO of your own health and take charge. And some things that women don't realize is that 80 percent of women diagnosed with breast cancer actually don't have a family history, and 90 percent of breast cancers are not associated with a breast cancer gene. So, you know, what can you do? Well, one, you have to stop the faucet on things you can control because we can't control our genes, right. So, that's like cleaning up your diet, lots of fruits and vegetables, the Mediterranean diet. And this isn't popular thing to say, but really limit or eliminate alcohol use. It's a carcinogen. Get moving and exercise. Be a squeaky wheel. You know, in terms of young women, 80 percent of them feel their breast lump themselves, right, so speak up, be aware of changes in your breasts and report them to your doctor, right.\par \par \uc2 DR. INE MENN (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 Know your family history, not just your mom's side but also your dad's side, and see if you should be referred for genetic testing. There's really great breast risk assessment tools that take into account breast density.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There are the things out there. Ask questions, all that. And know for your, you said you were diagnosed at 28. That had to be so terrifying. But here you are now, talking about it on TV, your post-breast cancer diagnosis daughter here watching. Full circle moment.\par \par \uc2 DR. INE MENN (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 She is.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That so much for being here with us, Dr. Menn. We appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 DR. INE MENN (OB/GYN)\par \par \uc2 Thank you so much for having me.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Gio, over to you.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Such an important conversation. Thank you guys.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241028ekac00065\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "THE OFFICE" STAR JENNA FISCHER'S PRIVATE CANCER BATTLE MOM OF TWO SHARES JOURNEY WITH "AGGRESSIVE" FORM OF BREAST CANCER\b0\par\par\uc2 689 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRACKING MILTON\par \par \uc2 MILTON, PREPARATION, LANDFALL, EVACUATION, CASTOR, RESIDENTS\par \par \uc2 MILTON, NATIONAL GUARDS, RESPONDERS, MOBILIZATION\par \par \uc2 MILTON, AIRPORTS, CLOSING, EVACUATIONS, GAS, ROADS\par \par \uc2 CRISWELL, MILTON, FEMA, PREPAREDNESS, HELENE\par \par \uc2 WOODWARD, "WAR", TRUMP, PUTIN, COVID, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 DOJ, \uc2 FBI\uc2 , TERROR PLOT, TAWHEDI, ARREST, \uc2 ISIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 MILTON, LANDFALL, SURGE, EVACUATION, WINDS\par \par \uc2 FAA\uc2 , BOEING, RUDDER, SAFETY, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 JETS, FIRED, SALEH, JOHNSON, RODGERS, ORLOVSKY\par \par \uc2 TROPICANA, VEGAS, IMPLOSION, KNOWLES, THORNDIKE, MIRAUL\par \par \uc2 WNBA, LYNX, LIBERTY, ELLIE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE MILTON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POTENTIAL INUNDATION\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE MILTON\par \par \uc2 TIKTOK, LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 CONJOINED TWINS, RUFFIN\par \par \uc2 FISCHER, CANCER\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back with another "GMA" cover story. "The Office" star Jenna Fischer revealed a private diagnosis of reveal a private battle with breast cancer, shared that she's now cancer free. Janai Norman back with her story. Hello, Janai.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "THE OFFICE" STAR JENNA FISCHER'S PRIVATE CANCER BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MOM OF TWO SHARES JOURNEY WITH "AGGRESSIVE" FORM OF BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George. A relief for her, a surprise to so many of us. Jenna Fischer worked, really worked hard to keep her diagnosis private. Speaking out now during breast cancer awareness month saying she's making the announcement for two reasons, one, she's ready to ditch the wigs, and two, quote, "to implore you to get your annual mammograms."\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM "THE OFFICE"\par \par \uc2 JENNA FISCHER ("THE OFFICE")\par \par \uc2 I came in early, I stayed late, and I doubled my sales last month.\par \par \uc2 ACTOR ("THE OFFICE")\par \par \uc2 Oh, really. From what, two to four?\par \par \uc2 JENNA FISCHER ("THE OFFICE")\par \par \uc2 Yep.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jenna Fischer, known, for her comedic chops as Pam on "The Office" posting on \uc2 Instagram\uc2  Tuesday, "last December I was diagnosed with stage one triple positive breast cancer. After completing surgery, chemotherapy and radiation, I'm now cancer free," writing her journey started last October with this post. "Reminder to schedule your mammogram." And a nod to this scene from season two of the hit show.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP OF "THE OFFICE"\par \par \uc2 STEVE CARELL ("THE OFFICE")\par \par \uc2 You should check yourself out. You know, give yourself an exam. Those things are like ticking time bags.\par \par \uc2 JENNA FISCHER ("THE OFFICE")\par \par \uc2 Stage 1 triple positive breast cancer we often find in younger women. This is a little bit more of an aggressive cancer, but it's also one that we have targeted drugs, particularly targeting that HER2 protein that are very effective and really improve curates.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The 50-year-old star acknowledging, "if I had waited six months longer, things could have been much worse." Thankful for her caregivers, family and friends, including "Office" and now podcast costar Angela Kinsey. Fischer saying, "for a long time she was the only person in my work space who knew. When I lost my hair, she wore hats to our work meetings so I wouldn't be the only one. When I needed a break, we took one." Fischer urging everyone to keep up with their mammograms, saying, "Michael was right. Get them checked, ladies. And know that, should you get a breast cancer diagnosis, there is a village waiting to care for you."\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, again she credits that early detection. You heard her there in the piece. She said if she'd waited six months it could have been so much worse. So she implores you not to skip your mammograms. It's recommended that women start getting annual exams at age 40. And find out if you have dense breasts. That can make it more difficult to detect breast cancer. You can request additional testing which can be critical and so lifesaving.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, it can. Yes.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It really can. It's so, so kind of her to become, go public with that.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yep. Not easy.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) With that, for an important message. Yeah. Not easy to do.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241024eka90003c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 29 DAYS TO ELECTION DAY TRUMP BARNSTORMING BATTLEGROUNDS AS HARRIS GOES ON MEDIA BLITZ\b0\par\par\uc2 571 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HURRICANE MILTON INTENSIFYING\par \par \uc2 MILTON, HELENE, DAMAGE, FLOODING, POWNALL\par \par \uc2 HELENE, RECOVERY, RESPONSE, TROOPS, RESIDENTS, CRISWELL\par \par \uc2 OCT 7TH, ISRAEL \uc2 HAMAS\uc2 , GAZA, ATTACK, SIEGEL, HOSTAGES\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, CAMPAIGN, MEDIA, ABORTION, MIDDLE EAST\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Matt Gutman, thanks. We're gonna get the latest now on the race for the White House. Just 29 days until the final votes. Former President Trump is barnstorming the battleground states. Vice President Harris is doing a m media blitz, sitting down for multiple interviews. She'll be marking the anniversary of the October 7th attack as well. Let's start with Mary Bruce, tracking the Harris campaign. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 29 DAYS TO ELECTION DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP BARNSTORMING BATTLEGROUNDS AS HARRIS GOES ON MEDIA BLITZ\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Well, the Vice President will mark the anniversary of the October 7th attack today by planting a memorial tree and delivering remarks later this afternoon. This all comes as Harris and her campaign are now shifting strategies, stepping up her engagement with the press through a wide array of interviews.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  kicking off a week long media blitz, doing multiple in depth interviews with the press, as the campaign enters the final sprint. Harris challenging \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on abortion rights on a podcast popular with young women, calling his false assertion that some states allow babies to be executed after birth, a bald face lie and dismissing Trump's claims to be a, quote, "Protector of women."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 ' MEDIA BLITZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP SITS DOWN FOR INTERVIEWS WITH TV NETWORKS & PODCASTS\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 There are now 20 states with Trump abortion bans, including bans that make no exception for rape or incest, which we just discussed. Which means that you're telling a survivor of a crime of a violation to their body they don't have a right to make a decision about what happens to their body next? Which is immoral. So this is the same guy that is now saying that? This is the same guy who said that women should be punished for having abortions.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) For weeks Harris has shied away from these kinds of interviews, even as her campaign's own data shows the more voters hear from her personally, the more they're likely to support her. But with 29 days to go, Harris this week appearing on podcasts, late night comedy shows and network news, including an interview with "60 Minutes."\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Harris forced to defend the Biden administration's record on the war in the Middle East. Asked why Israeli Prime Minister Netanyahu doesn't seem to be listening to the US.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The work that we have done has resulted in a number of movements in that region by Israel that were very much prompted by or a result of many things including our advocacy for what needs to happen in the region.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now, in addition to podcasts and that "60 Minutes" interview, Harris will also be on "The View" here on ABC, and participate in a Univision town hall out in Las Vegas, before campaigning in battleground Arizona. Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241023eka70002x\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Date\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctl